Expr_pattern : "Expr10003"
GO_term	"GO:0035861"
Gene	"WBGene00022172"
Reference	"WBPaper00040938"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00022172"
Reporter_gene
Subcellular_localization	"GFP:: COSA-1 is detected as a diffuse nucleoplasmic signal beginning in early pachytene and then displays a striking localization pattern later in pachytene that is consistent with expectations for a protein that marks crossover (CO) sites. Starting at the transition from mid to late pachytene and persisting through diplotene, GFP::COSA-1 localizes to 6.0 &plusmn; 0.2 bright foci per nucleus (n = 76), corresponding in number to the six COs - one per chromosome pair - that form during wild-type meiosis. At diplotene, GFP::COSA-1 localizes at the site of the single emerging chiasma on each homolog pair. We conclude that COSA-1 localizes to CO sites."
Transgene	"WBTransgene00031332"

Expr_pattern : "Expr10004"
