GO_term	"GO:0005634"
Gene	"WBGene00001831"
Reference	"WBPaper00040969"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00001831"
Reporter_gene
Subcellular_localization	"GFP:CeCENP-A is present in the nuclei of all embryonic cells. In the maternal germline, CeCENP-A is removed from chromosomes as they enter the pachytene stage of meiotic prophase, and is reloaded when nuclei progress into diplotene . CeCENP-A was not detected in the nuclei of mature sperm, and quantitative immunoblotting indicated that sperm have fewer than the detection limit of 300 CeCENP-A molecules."
Transgene	"WBTransgene00031336"

