Expr_pattern : "Expr10203"
GO_term	"GO:0005737"
GO_term	"GO:0060473"
Gene	"WBGene00004269"
Reference	"WBPaper00041559"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00004269"
Reporter_gene
Subcellular_localization	"RAB-6.1 temporarily co-localized with separase on the cortical granules for a few minutes and then was dispersed in the cytoplasm concomitantly with membrane fusion. RAB-6.1 co-localized with RAB-11.1 near the cortex until cortical granule secretion. RAB-6.1 and RAB-6.2 co-localized to vesicular structures throughout the oocyte cytoplasm. The vesicles were adjacent to the Golgi marker ManS suggesting that RAB-6.1\/RAB-6.2 vesicles are derived from the Golgi complex."
Transgene	"WBTransgene00031357"

Expr_pattern : "Expr10204"
GO_term	"GO:0005737"
Gene	"WBGene00004270"
Reference	"WBPaper00041559"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00004270"
Reporter_gene
Subcellular_localization	"RAB-6.1 and RAB-6.2 co-localized to vesicular structures throughout the oocyte cytoplasm. The vesicles were adjacent to the Golgi marker ManS suggesting that RAB-6.1\/RAB-6.2 vesicles are derived from the Golgi complex."
Transgene	"WBTransgene00031358"

Expr_pattern : "Expr10205"
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0005792" Certain
GO_term	"GO:0005769"
GO_term	"GO:0055037"
Gene	"WBGene00000424"
Pattern	"GFP- CED-10 localized strongly to the apical domain of intestinal epithelial cells (likely to the microvilli)."
Reference	"WBPaper00041307"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00000424"
Reporter_gene
Subcellular_localization	"GFP-CED-10 localized to intracellular puncta in the cytoplasm. The authors identified the intracellular puncta labeled by CED-10 as endosomes by performing a series of colocalization studies with a previously established set of intestine-specific compartment markers. CED-10 appeared specifically enriched on endosomes along the early and recycling pathway. Direct overlap of intestinal GFP-CED-10-labeled puncta and a subset of early endosomes marked by RFP-RAB-5 was observed. GFP-CED-10 showed the strongest colocalization with recycling endosome marker RFP-RAB-10, and displayed less overlap with later acting recycling endosome protein RFP-RME-1. Little overlap was observed between GFP-CED-10 and markers for late endosomes (GFP-RAB-7), the Golgi (MANS-GFP), or multi-vesicular bodies (GFP-HGRS-1\/Hrs) indicating specificity in endosome-type associated with CED-10."
Transgene	"WBTransgene00031359"

Expr_pattern : "Expr10206"
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0005792" Certain
GO_term	"GO:0005769"
GO_term	"GO:0055037"
Gene	"WBGene00000426"
Reference	"WBPaper00041307"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00000426"
Reporter_gene
Subcellular_localization	"CED-12-RFP colocalized well with GFP-CED-10 to the intracellular puncta in the cytoplasm. However, CED-12-RFP also strongly labeled a subapical band that displayed significant overlap with the GFP-CED-10 labeled apical band.Colocalization between CED-12-GFP and markers of early endosomes and recycling endosomes was observed."
Transgene	"WBTransgene00031360"

Expr_pattern : "Expr10207"
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0008378" Certain
Gene	"WBGene00018607"
Life_stage	"WBls:0000003"
Life_stage	"WBls:0000023"
Life_stage	"WBls:0000041"
Pattern	"Using semi-quantitative RT-PCR, we show that F48E3.8 is somatically expressed. F48E3.8 was first detected at 24 h following hatching, when grown at 25 C.F48E3.8 continued to be expressed at 48 h and 72 h. Adults first appeared at the 72 h time point and F48E3.8 showed clear expression despite the significant attenuation of the germline.F48E3.8 expression persisted through to 120 h. F48E3.8 was expressed in the absence of a germline and it appeared to persist into adulthood. All three predicted transcripts of F48E3.8 include sequence coding for the PDA domain. The demonstration of F48E3.8 expression in larval and adult stages contrasts with in situ data that showed expression was restricted to embryos (NEXTDB, http:\/\/nematode.lab.nig.ac.jp\/). This may reflect increased sensitivity afforded by RT-PCR or differences in expression of alternative transcripts of F48E3.8."
RT_PCR	"Primers: CCTTCAAGACTTCTGACCGAATGCCCG (F) GTTTGTGGCCAATATGGGCTGCTGACC (R)"
RT_PCR
Reference	"WBPaper00041310"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00018607"

