Pattern	"The nlg-1 promoter expressed GFP in cholinergic motor neurons but not in GABAergic neurons."
Reference	"WBPaper00041363"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00006412"
Reporter_gene	"The transcriptional reporter for nlg-1 used 6.5kb of 5' flanking sequence. A 2.4kb myo-3 myosin promoter was used for expression in body muscles, a 3.2kb unc-17 VAChT promoter was used for expression in cholinergic neurons, and a 2.6kb unc-129 promoter was used for expression in DA and DB motor neurons."
Reporter_gene
Subcellular_localization	"When expressed in cholinergic DA and DB motor neurons, NLG-1::GFP exhibited a punctate distribution in dorsal cord axons but was diffuse in ventral cord dendrites. Dorsal cord NLG-1 puncta co-localized with a synaptic vesicle (SV) marker (mCherry-tagged UNC-57 endophilin). NRX-1::GFP expressed in body muscles was also punctate in the nerve cords and these NRX-1 puncta were often closely apposed to pre-synaptic UNC-57 puncta."
Transgene	"WBTransgene00015243"

