GO_term	"GO:0043025"
Gene	"WBGene00004457"
Pattern	"In transgenic animals that overexpressed the functional RPM-1::GFP, both the anti-RPM-1 and anti-GFP antibodies gave identical patterns and showed that RPM-1::GFP was localized in distinct subcellular regions of the nervous system. Strong RPM-1::GFP expression was seen in the nerve ring and nerve cords but not in commissural processes that do not form synapses. Costained the transgenic animals with anti-SNT-1 antibodies and anti-GFP antibodies and analysis of confocal images revealed that RPM-1::GFP was localized adjacent to SNT-1 in presynaptic terminals. Coexpression of RPM-1 and SNB-1::GFP in the GABAergic DD and VD neurons specifically found that RPM-1 and SNB-1::GFP were present in nonoverlapping regions at individual GABAergic NMJs."
Reference	"WBPaper00004146"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00004457"
