Subcellular_localization	"During oocyte maturation, cytoplasmic separase rapidly accumulated in the nucleus on homologous chromosomes. Separase also localized to unusual filaments distributed throughout the cortex. Before anaphase onset, separase was lost from these filamentous structures and accumulated on cortical vesicles. Separase co-localized with WGA-labeled cortical granules during anaphase I. Separase-labeled vesicles were lost during anaphase I, beginning in the region near the meiotic spindle. In mitotic embryos, separase localized to centrosomes, chromosomes and a diffuse cloud around the metaphase plate and anaphase spindle."
