Pattern	"The prig-6RIG-6::GFP construct drives expression of all RIG-6	isoforms in fusion with GFP, under their endogenous promoter. rig-6 expression is detected during embryogenesis and is maintained throughout adulthood. rig-6 is	expressed in I1 and I3 pharyngeal interneurons, NSM motor	neurons and other unidentified head neurons. RIG-6::GFP is also localized in the cell bodies and axons of different subtypes of VNC motorneurons, in the	HSN and the CAN neurons. Neuronal expression of	rig-6 also includes the ALM and PLM touch	receptor neurons. Non-neuronal cells expressing rig-6 include somatic muscles and the hypodermis. We also	detected rig-6 expression in the developing and adult EC."
