Pattern	"At the comma stage embryo, faint lin-12(2in_490) fluorescence is detected in	cells that are located ventrally along the anteroposterior body axis.	These cells represent P blast precursors. At the L1-L2 stages, lin-12(2in_490) was abundantly expressed in the ventral nerve cord. Most, if not all, ventral nerve cord neurons expressed lin-12(2in_490), and both neurons and axonal bundles were	glowing. These cells maintained a robust lin-12(2in_490) expression	throughout larval development."
Reference	"WBPaper00041920"
Reporter_gene
Transgene	"WBTransgene00018125"

