Pattern	"TCER-1::GFP was present in all germ cell nuclei, starting from the mitotic cells at the distal end to the oocytes at the proximal end of the gonad. TCER-1::mCherry showed an identical expression pattern (data not shown). Both of these transgenes were expressed in somatic nuclei as well (data not shown). TCER-1 reporter fusions were present at the inner periphery of the nucleus, often in a crescent-shaped fashion. However, we did not detect any fluorescence signal corresponding to either of the TCER-1 reporter fusions in the cytoplasm."
Reference	"WBPaper00042071"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00022855"
