Life_stage	"WBls:0000023"
Life_stage	"WBls:0000041"
Reference	"WBPaper00005828"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00002275"
Subcellular_localization	"Double-immunofluorescence staining of C. elegans with antibodies against the endogenous Ce-lamin and Ce-MAN1 showed that they colocalized at the nuclear periphery throughout embryonic, larval, and adult development. Ce-MAN1 is expressed in all cell types examined and may be ubiquitous in C. elegans. By immunogold electron microscopy, a C-terminal epitope of Ce-MAN1 localized near the nuclear inner membrane and remained associated with peripheral chromatin and Ce-lamin in detergent-extracted nuclei."

Expr_pattern : "Expr1088"
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0003681" Certain
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0005319" Certain
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0005813" Certain
Antibody	"Rabbit polyclonal antibodies to HSP25."
Antibody
Antibody_info	"WBAntibody00000270"
GO_term	"GO:0031430"
GO_term	"GO:0055120"
Gene	"WBGene00002023"
Pattern	"In both larvae and adults, strong staining was observed in body wall muscle and in the lining of the pharynx. The pharyngeal staining is localized to a subset of cells bordering the lumen. strong HSP25 staining was also observed at the junctions between cells forming the spermathecal wall. HSP25 appears to be associated with desmosomes in the spermatheca."
Reference	"WBPaper00003970"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00002023"
Remark	"When an excess of recombinant HSP25 was included in the reactions as competitor, no staining was observed, indicating that the pattern seen is specific to HSP25."
Subcellular_localization	"In body wall muscle, HSP25 was localized to a series of thin lines parallel to the long axis of the muscle fiber, alternating with thicker lines consisting of discrete spots. This pattern is consistent with the localization of HSP25 to the dense bodies and M-lines of the myofibrils."

