Subcellular_localization	"As previously reported, HDA-1 in wild-type animals is detected in most or all cells of the body, including cells of the nervous system (Dufourcq et al., 2002). The protein is concentrated in nuclei (Dufourcq et al., 2002), but, unlike in the previous report, prominent staining was also detected within neuronal processes."

