Pattern	"In wild-type worm, KLF-3 protein was undetectable in embryos. However, KLF-3 expression was evident in all larval stages, as well as in adult. Microscopic observation of animals at larval and adult stages showed that level of KLF-3 expression was constant in each developmental stage. Throughout worm development, the anti-KLF-3 antibodies detected KLF-3 protein in the intestine, where it was most abundant. We also observed KLF-3 protein in both arms of the germline."
Reference	"WBPaper00042349"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00003480"

