Pattern	"Animals carrying rol-3::GFP as a transgenic array (sEx1594) express GFP in all major hypodermal nuclei, with the exception of the seam cells. Expression is first detected during dorsal intercalation and is particularly intense throughout embryogenesis. Upon hatching rol-3::GFP expression persists in the major hypodermis at a relatively low-level throughout development up until the adult stage, where expression is not detected."
Reference	"WBPaper00042458"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00004395"
Reporter_gene
Transgene	"WBTransgene00018324"

Expr_pattern : "Expr11037"
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0005733" Certain
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0005753" Certain
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0007809" Certain
GO_term	"GO:0031252"
GO_term	"GO:0071944"
Gene	"WBGene00004395"
Life_stage	"WBls:0000003"
Life_stage	"WBls:0000023"
Reference	"WBPaper00042458"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00004395"
Reporter_gene
Subcellular_localization	"Consistent with the transcriptional GFP reporter ROL-3::GFP is expressed in the major hypodermal cells and excluded from seam cells. At the point when seam cells are quiescent ROL-3::GFP expression is generally diffuse across the surface of the major hypodermis. Prior to and during seam cell division however, ROL-3::GFP expression intensifies and accumulates in foci at the seam cell boundaries. ROL-3::GFP localization at the seam cell boundary is lost at the anterior seam cells as they fuse with the major hypodermis. Particularly intense ROL-3::GFP foci are observed at the leading edges of the posterior seam cells as they elongate towards one another. ROL-3 localization at the seam cell boundary persists until seam cell elongation is completed. In addition to the major hypodermal cells ROL-3::GFP expression is also detected in the anterior seam cells as they take on the major hypodermal fate at the L1 stage of development. These cells migrate to separate the vulval precursor cells (VPCs) which also express ROL-3::GFP at this stage. Expression of ROL-3::GFP in the VPC's is restricted to L1 larval stage, being rapidly reduced during the L1-L2 transition and not detected at latter stages of development."
Transgene	"WBTransgene00018325"

Expr_pattern : "Expr11038"
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0005733" Certain
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0005735" Certain
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0005753" Certain
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0005755" Certain
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0006748" Certain
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0008074" Certain
Gene	"WBGene00011522"
Pattern	"A transcriptional GFP reporter driven by the putative srap-1 promoter is detected in a variety of tissues including the major hypodermis and seam cells. Notable expression of this reporter is also observed in the tissues of the developing vulva and central nervous system. Expression of SRAP-1::GFP translational fusion is detected at the surface of the newly synthesized cuticle coincident with the molt. Significant accumulation of SRAP-1::GFP is also detected at the seam syncytium in the adult stage."
Reference	"WBPaper00042458"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00011522"
Reporter_gene
Transgene	"WBTransgene00018483"

