Reporter_gene
Subcellular_localization	"EPN-1::GFP, regardless expressed from Pepn-1 or Pced-1, is localized to both the cytoplasm and plasma membrane. In the cytoplasm, EPN-1::GFP is either evenly distributed or associated with puncta that likely represent intracellular organelles. In embryos, EPN-1::GFP is enriched on extending pseudopods and remains on the surfaces of nascent phagosomes for 4-6 minutes before disappearing."
Transgene	"WBTransgene00018831"

