Gene	"WBGene00001519"
Pattern	"In transgenic animals expressing Pgar-3::gfp, fluorescence was detected in body wall and pharynx muscles, as well as in motor neurons	of	the ventral	nerve	cord. GFP fluorescence was detected in all cholinergic motor neurons of the ventral nerve cord but not in GABAergic motor neurons."
Reference	"WBPaper00044110"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00001519"
Reporter_gene
Subcellular_localization	"GAR-3-GFP fluorescence was not detected in axons in single-copy transgenic animals (0 of 15 axons) and was rarely detected in axons of multicopy animals (3 of 23 axons). GAR-3-GFP was also not detected in dendrites of single-copy transgenic animals, and was occasionally detected in proximal dendrites of multicopy animals (data not shown). When axonal or dendritic GAR-3-GFP fluorescence was detected, it adopted a diffuse	pattern	of localization. Based on these results, the authors conclude that GAR-3 is highly enriched in cholinergic motor neuron cell bodies, where it asymmetrically distributes to the dorsal surfaces, but is likely to be very low or absent from neuronal processes."
Subcellular_localization	"GAR-3-GFP fluorescence was observed in the ventral nerve cord and in motor neuron cell bodies in discrete patches that run parallel to the ventral nerve cord. In motor neurons, GAR-3-GFP primarily localized to narrow regions that extended longitudinally along the dorsal side of each motor neuron cell body. This pattern is suggestive of cell surface localization of GAR-3-GFP because the fluorescent regions were found on the outer edge of cell bodies marked by soluble mCherry. Similar localization patterns were observed in DA\/DB motor neurons of animals expressing single-copy GAR-3-gfp (by MosSCI insertion of Punc-129::GAR-3-gfp). In body wall muscles, GAR-3-GFP fluorescence was also asymmetrically distributed at sites of contact between muscle cells, on muscle arms, and in postsynaptic regions where muscle arms contact the dorsal and ventral nerve cords."
Subcellular_localization	"GAR-3-GFP localization was not asymmetric early in development (asymmetry ratio 1.19 +\/- 0.6 in the L3 stage), but it became asymmetric starting at the L4 stage (3.25 +\/- 0.34) and maintained asymmetry in adults. GAR-3-GFP on muscle membranes was visible in young animals (L3 stage) and appeared enhanced in older animals."
Transgene	"WBTransgene00018745"
Transgene	"WBTransgene00018746"
Transgene	"WBTransgene00018894"

