Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00011648"
Reporter_gene
Subcellular_localization	"CNI-1 and GLR-1 were in close apposition to SEC-24\/COPII puncta, which mark putative ER export sites."
Subcellular_localization	"CNI-1 was also expressed in the processes of AVA, where it was distributed in a punctate pattern that colocalized with the ER\/Golgi marker, PISY-1. The punctate colocalization of GLR-1 with CNI-1 suggests that CNI-1 might also function at synapses and that is expressed on the cell surface. Surface expression of CNI-1 was also supported by in vivo antibody labeling experiments. These results indicate that CNI-1 is not restricted to the cell body or intracellular organelles and that CNI-1 is present at synapses."
Subcellular_localization	"In neuronal cell bodies, CNI-1::GFP appeared punctate and distinctively clustered at perinuclear sites, suggestive of localization to the ER. By colocalization studies the authors confirmed that CNI-1 is expressed in discrete regions of the ER\/Golgi where it colocalized with GLR-1."
Transgene	"WBTransgene00019052"

