Gene	"WBGene00003760"
Life_stage	"WBls:0000023"
Pattern	"NLP-22 is selectively expressed, in a single-neuron pair, the RIAs. NLP-22 is predicted to be secreted. When GFP was fused to the C-terminus of the NLP-22 preproprotein, green fluorescence was observed in several neurons in the head as well as in the ventral nerve cord, supporting the notion that NLP-22 is a secreted peptide."
Pattern	"mRNA abundance of the gene nlp-22 was higher in the L4 stage than in lethargus. Using qRT-PCR, we confirmed that nlp-22 mRNA expression cycles with a constant phase relationship to lethargus. nlp-22 mRNA peaked midway through the active larval stages, decreased during each lethargus stage, and was absent in adults."
RT_PCR
Reference	"WBPaper00044546"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00003760"
Reporter_gene	"[pnlp-22::GFP] transcriptional fusion and [Pnlp-22::nlp-22:gfp; Pmyo-2::mCherry; unc-119(+)] translational fusion. The transcriptional reporter for nlp-22 (Pnlp-22:Intron:gfp) was made by fusing the promoter of nlp-22 (-450 to +3) to the coding sequence of GFP, amplified from pPD95.75 and replacing one of the synthetic introns of gfp with the intron of nlp-22( +85 to +481)."
Reporter_gene
Transgene	"WBTransgene00019305"

