Pattern	"plr-1 expression was observed in a subset of head, ventral nerve cord and tail neurons as well as in the excretory canal and tail epidermis. In particular, expression was observed in DB, NSM, RIF or RIG, PHC, CAN, HSN, and VC. Transient expression was detected in AVG during early larval development and late embryogenesis, which is when AVG differentiates. The mechanosensory neurons ALM, AVM, PLM and PVM respond to Wnts and do not express PLR-1."
Reference	"WBPaper00044679"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00023404"
Reporter_gene
Subcellular_localization	"When co-expressed in AVG, most PLR-1-mCherry puncta are colabeled with the late endosomal marker RME-8-GFP and some PLR-1-GFP vesicles are marked by the early endosomal reporter mRFP-EEA-1. A few PLR-1 vesicles are co-labeled with the Golgi marker MANS-YFP, but none are marked by the lysosomal reporter LMP-1-GFP. Thus, PLR-1 accumulates primarily in endosomes."
Transgene	"WBTransgene00031623"

