Gene	"WBGene00003001"
Pattern	"LIN-12::GFP is present and membrane-localized in all SM sub-lineage cells from the 2-SM stage through the 8-SM stage. At the 16-SM stage the expression of LIN-12::GFP becomes restricted to the four SM descendants that are fated to become VM2s. As these cells begin to differentiate into VM2s, LIN-12::GFP becomes nuclear localized. Thus LIN-12 is present and activated in cells fated to become VM2s. LIN-12 is present in M.vlpaaap, M.vlpaapa, M.vrpaaap and M.vrpaapa cells."
Reference	"WBPaper00044842"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00003001"
Reporter_gene
Transgene	"WBTransgene00000048"

Expr_pattern : "Expr11591"
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0005784" Certain
GO_term	"GO:0005634"
Gene	"WBGene00020466"
Pattern	"SLD-2:: GFP is expressed in the distal tip and loop region of the germline. SLD-2 localization is strictly limited to the proliferative nuclei of the C. elegans germline."
Reference	"WBPaper00044861"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00020466"
Reporter_gene
Subcellular_localization	"SLD-2::GFP revealed localization to the majority of nuclei in the mitotic zone of the germline, regardless of cell cycle stage. Similarly, it was observed in early embryonic cell cycles that SLD-2 is nuclear from as soon as the nuclear membrane forms after mitosis until nuclear envelope breakdown in the next mitosis, suggesting that nuclear localization of SLD-2 is not regulated during the mitotic cell cycle. Interestingly, however, SLD-2::GFP localization ends abruptly at the meiotic transition zone, as determined by the virtual absence of GFP signal in the crescent-shaped meiotic nuclei. Although absent from the meiotic region of the germline, SLD-2::GFP reappears in developing oocyte nuclei in the loop region of the gonad and in mature oocytes."
Transgene	"WBTransgene00019624"

