Expr_pattern : "Expr1160"
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0004575" Certain
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0004576" Certain
Antibody	"Polyclonal antisera against NOS-1 fusion protein expressed in E. coli."
Antibody
Antibody_info	"WBAntibody00000246"
Gene	"WBGene00003783"
Life_stage	"WBls:0000010"
Life_stage	"WBls:0000013"
Life_stage	"WBls:0000015"
Life_stage	"WBls:0000021"
Pattern	"NOS-1 protein is expressed sequentially during embryogenesis. No NOS-1 protein was detected in pregastrulation embryos, even though nos-1 RNA is present in these stages. NOS-1 first appeared in Z2 and Z3 at the 550-cell stage and remained expressed in these cells until the end of embryogenesis."
Reference	"WBPaper00003762"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00003783"
Remark	"The specificity of antibody was confirmed by staining embryos deficient for NOS-1. Affinity-purified anti-NOS-1 antibody detected NOS-1 in nos-2(RNAi) embryos but not in nos-1(RNAi) and nos-1(gv5) embryos. NOS-1 and NOS-2 thus do not depend on each other for expression."
Remark	"To test whether NOS-1 is expressed zygotically, authors crossed nos-1(gv5) hermaphrodites (which express no NOS-1) to wild-type males and stained their progeny for NOS-1 protein. Detected NOS-1 expression in a pattern identical to that observed in embryos derived from wild-type hermaphrodites, confirming that NOS-1 expression is zygotic."

