Subcellular_localization	"PTRN-1a translational fusions localized to small, closely spaced puncta throughout neurites. Irregularly spaced puncta of PTRN-1a::tdTomato were observed throughout the PVD dendrites and axon. Often, continuous PTRN-1::tdTomato fluorescence was observed in the primary dendrite adjacent to the cell body, and fewer, farther spaced puncta in the quaternary processes.In the PHC dendrite, PTRN-1::tdTomato localized to puncta with spacing similar to that of the PVD neuron, suggestive that the PTRN-1a localization pattern in neurites is similar across different neuron classes."
