Pattern	"Pcwn-2::mCherry signal first appeared in the intestine before the expression of Punc-25::GFP during embryogenesis. At late embryonic stage when RMED\/V neurite start extending posteriorly, the highest expression of CWN-2 is found at posterior pharyngneal bulb and the pharyngeal-intestinal valve. When animals are at L1 stage, the RMED\/V neurites grow towards the posterior pharynx, where CWN-2 displays relatively higher expression level. The expression pattern of CWN-2 at both embryonic and L1 stages correlates well with the attractant role of CWN-2 during neurite outgrowth. After L1 stage, the neurites continue their growth and pass the posterior pharynx; meanwhile CWN-2 is also found expressed in body muscles and some ventral cord neurons."
Reference	"WBPaper00037046"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00000858"
Remark	"Temporal description."
