Gene	"WBGene00007110"
Life_stage	"WBls:0000003"
Pattern	"mCherry::LEO-1 was detected in the nuclei of virtually all cells throughout embryogenesis from the one-cell stage."
Reference	"WBPaper00045133"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00007110"
Remark	"Temporal description."
Reporter_gene
Subcellular_localization	"mCherry::LEO-1 was not uniformly present within the nuclei, but enriched in discrete nuclear regions. Its localization varied during the cell cycle. Before mitosis, the intense mCherry::LEO-1 signal was detected within the nuclei. Upon mitotic nuclear envelope breakdown (NEBD), the nuclear mCherry::LEO-1 signal apparently diffused within the cytoplasm. During metaphase through anaphase, mCherry::LEO-1 was not detected on condensed chromosomes. In telophase when nuclear envelope is reassembled, mCherry::LEO-1 signal became detectable again in the nuclei."
Transgene	"WBTransgene00019926"

