Pattern	"Expression is first seen in precomma stage embryos, in as yet unidentified nuclei. In comma stage embryos staining is seen in the intestinal precursors, and other cells including possibly members of the C cell lineage. In 3-fold embryos and through till L3 stage larvae, expression appears as pairs of nuclei down the body starting anteriorly of the metacorpus, probably hyp-7. There is also a lot of diffuse staining in the head and pharynx. In larvae strong expression is seen in the intestinal nuclei. At L4 stage this expression starts to fade, and fewer nuclei are seen to stain. In adults the expression is reduced to a handful of nuclei (from 1-10) around the pharynx. Sometimes in adults a few anterior intestinal nuclei continue to show expression."
