Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00006379"
Reporter_gene
Subcellular_localization	"Between divisions, SYS-1 localizes weakly to the cortex and cytoplasm. Prior to metaphase, SYS-1 localizes to the nucleus and cytoplasm. During metaphase and anaphase, SYS-1 localizes to bright puncta that behave similarly to centrosomes. Centrosomal localization was confirmed by colocalizing mCherry::SYS-1 with GFP-tagged beta-tubulin, consistent with SYS-1 centrosomal localization observed in other tissues (Phillips et al., 2007; Huang et al., 2007). Asymmetric localization of SYS-1 is established during early telophase when SYS-1 levels are rapidly lowered in the anterior daughter while SYS-1 levels increase in the nuclear region of the posterior daughter. SYS-1 asymmetry is maintained after cytokinesis into late telophase when it localizes primarily to the nucleus of the posterior daughter. Within an hour after division, nuclear SYS-1 decreases and localization increases at the cortex and cytoplasm, but SYS-1 eventually becomes undetectable two hours after division."
Transgene	"WBTransgene00001921"

Expr_pattern : "Expr11813"
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0005733" Certain
GO_term	"GO:0005737"
GO_term	"GO:0030056"
GO_term	"GO:0071944"
Gene	"WBGene00010776"
Life_stage	"WBls:0000015"
Pattern	"Confocal microscopy analysis revealed that during early elongation, PIX-1::GFP is expressed in the dorsal, lateral and ventral hypodermal cells. Throughout early elongation, PIX-1::GFP is located at the trans-epithelial attachment structures (hemidesmosomes) in dorsal and ventral hypodermal cells, as previously reported and is also homogeneously distributed in the cytoplasm and at the cell periphery of all expressing cells. Interestingly, at the comma stage, PIX-1::GFP expression appears to be reduced in several posterior dorsal hypodermal cells. Concomitant with the fusion of these cells, around the 1.2-fold stage, the expression of PIX-1::GFP appears to be reduced in the fused cells."
Reference	"WBPaper00045130"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00010776"
Reporter_gene
Subcellular_localization	"Confocal microscopy analysis revealed that during early elongation, PIX-1::GFP is expressed in the dorsal, lateral and ventral hypodermal cells. Throughout early elongation, PIX-1::GFP is located at the trans-epithelial attachment structures (hemidesmosomes) in dorsal and ventral hypodermal cells, as previously reported and is also homogeneously distributed in the cytoplasm and at the cell periphery of all expressing cells. Interestingly, at the comma stage, PIX-1::GFP expression appears to be reduced in several posterior dorsal hypodermal cells. Concomitant with the fusion of these cells, around the 1.2-fold stage, the expression of PIX-1::GFP appears to be reduced in the fused cells."
Transgene	"WBTransgene00020094"

