Subcellular_localization	"Ran localized mainly to the nucleus and the nuclear envelope during interphase. At prometaphase, Ran still localized to the nuclear envelope. When the nuclear envelope began to disassemble at M phase (early metaphase), Ran localized throughout the entire cell. At late metaphase, Ran was found to localize to the outer edges of each chromosome, which correspond to kinetochore regions. The localization of Ran to kinetochore regions persisted until anaphase. At telophase, Ran was no more detected at kinetochore regions. Instead, it localized around the decondensing chromosomes."

