Pattern	"In five independent reporter lines generated, fluorescence was regularly observed in the ALA interneuron. In addition, variable reporter expression was observed in cholinergic motor neurons in the ventral nerve cord but not in GABA motor neurons of the ventral nerve cord. Rather, the vav-1 reporter was expressed in two GABA motor neurons in the head, known as RME dorsal and RME ventral, which regulate head oscillations. Several cell types were found to be negative for vav-1 reporter expression. The tested vav-1 reporters did not show co-expression with markers of dopaminergic neurons (Pdat-1::GFP), command interneurons of the locomotory circuit, which directly activate motor neurons (Pglr-1::RFP) or with a marker of a small set of sensory neurons (AWC and ASE neurons, marked by Pceh-36::RFP). In sum, fluorescent vav-1 reporters are expressed in a small subset of neurons that comprise multiple cell types, including an interneuron, cholinergic motor neurons and a small subset of GABAergic motor neurons."
Reference	"WBPaper00046036"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00006887"
Reporter_gene
Transgene	"WBTransgene00020566"

Expr_pattern : "Expr12084"
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0003955" Certain
GO_term	"GO:0043025"
Gene	"WBGene00006887"
Reference	"WBPaper00046036"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00006887"
Reporter_gene
Subcellular_localization	"VAV-1::GFP is localized to the cell body of ALA, but not in the nucleus. VAV- 1::GFP was not observed in the axons along the length of the animal. These data indicate that VAV-1 does not associate with synaptic or dense-core vesicles or their release sites within ALA."
Transgene	"WBTransgene00020566"

