Reporter_gene
Subcellular_localization	"The GFP signal is concentrated in puncta spread throughout the cytoplasm mainly in the cell body, but also extends into neuronal processes. The punctate expression of PLR-1::GFP fusion protein suggests that PLR-1 is present in some endocytotic compartments. Recently PLR-1 has been shown to colocalize with endosomal markers (Moffat et al., 2014, Expr11480), suggesting that PLR-1 indeed enters the secretory pathway."
Transgene	"WBTransgene00031719"

