Pattern	"Eggs already showed the corresponding GFP fluorescence, with more and more tissues following during development (L1 larval stage: pharynx, excretory cell, some sensory neurons; L2-L4 larval stages: intestine, rectal sensory neurons; adult worms: longitudinal muscles, gonads). The rare males showed GFP expression in their spermathecae. Within the anterior part of the nervous system, GFP expression was detected in the pharyngeal nerve ring and in some sensory neurons. Within its posterior part, lumbar ganglia and the dorso-rectal ganglion showed GFP expression."
Reference	"WBPaper00046151"
