Pattern	"Wild-type transgenic animals showed a constant expression of pxn-1 throughout their development, starting from the egg and continuing through to the adult stages. The expression patterns were associated with the ventral nerve cord (VNC), the dorsal nerve cord (DNC), body wall muscles, neurons, vulval muscles, uterine muscles, head neurons, intestine, and hypodermis. Moreover, the patterns were observed in excretory cells and in the spermathecal-uterine valve."
Reference	"WBPaper00046086"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00004256"
Reporter_gene
Transgene	"WBTransgene00031740"

Expr_pattern : "Expr12147"
GO_term	"GO:0031012"
Gene	"WBGene00004256"
Reference	"WBPaper00046086"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00004256"
Reporter_gene
Subcellular_localization	"PXN-1::GFP is localized in extracellular matrix. PXN-1::GFP expressed all along the body of the animal, but the expression was more distinctly found in the muscle-muscle attachment regions. PXN-2::mCherry expressed in regions somewhat different from those that were found to express PXN-1. Specifically, PXN-1::GFP expression localized between body wall muscle cells, but such expression was not observed for PXN-2::mCherry. PXN-1 and PXN-2 were localized in the coelomocytes and PXN-2 was found in the hypodermis. Interestingly, PXN-1::GFP was distributed along the pharynx, which signifies that PXN-1 may function in the attachments between pharynx and hypodermis. In addition, since PXN-1 and PXN-2 were both localized to the coelomocytes, it appears that both are likely secretory proteins."
Transgene	"WBTransgene00031741"

