Pattern	"To identify npr-2-expressing cells, we generated transgenic animals expressing GFP under control of the rescuing npr-2 promoter and identified a total of 15-17 GFP-positive neurons that likely express npr-2. These neurons include sensory neurons OLQs (2-4), ASHL\/R, ADFL\/R, FLPL\/R, and PVDL\/R and interneurons AIZL\/R, SABD, and PVQL\/R. The expressivity of the npr-2p::GFP transgene in each class of neurons ranges from 62.5% for the AIZ interneurons and 100% for the FLP sensory neurons. The variable penetrance of GFP expression in these neurons might be caused by transgene mosaicism or variable GFP expression intensity."
