Pattern	"Animals carrying the mir-48::gfp construct showed temporal expression in the hypodermal seam cells two stages earlier than its let-7 homologues at the L2 stage. mir-48 was not detected in the gonad at any stage. specific expression of mir-48 was observed in the P5.p and P7.p cells that will assume 2 vulval cell fates. It is interesting to note that expression of mir-237, mir-84, and mir-48 was absent in the P6.p cell during the mid- to late L3 stage, and expression of mir-237 and mir-84 but not mir-48 was present in the anchor cell."
Reference	"WBPaper00026854"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00003039"
