Pattern	"During embryogenesis, at the pre-comma stage, the GFP signal was first observed in the RID precursor (ABalappaap) before its final round of cell division. After the division, GFP signals were observed in both progenies. After the RID sister cell had undergone programmed cell death, the RID terminal differentiation marker Pceh-10::wCherry was observed in the surviving cell. Coexpression of the ceh-10 and unc-3 reporters in the RID neuron persisted into the larval stage. Similar to what has been reported previously (Prasad et al., 1998, 2008; Kratsios et al., 2012), the unc-3 fosmid reporter also exhibited expression in cholinergic motor neurons."
Reference	"WBPaper00046563"
