Subcellular_localization	"The SOR-1 antibody staining pattern was consistent with those shown by the gfp reporter (Expr12373). SOR-1 is nuclear localized and expressed in all cells from the one-cell stage onwards. As development proceeds, the expression level of SOR-1 appears to decline. From the two cell-stage onwards, SOR-1 is found to be inhomogenously expressed in the nuclei with obvious accumulations in distinct nuclear speckles. During larval development, SOR-1 is present in all somatic cell nuclei. Although at lower levels of expression, the nuclear bodies in which it localizes can still be formed."

