Pattern	"TSP-21::GFP is plasma membrane-localized and is expressed in a wide variety of somatic cell types, including the pharynx, intestine and hypodermis starting in embryos after the 100 cell stage and peaking in L1 and L2 larvae. The TSP-21::GFP signal in these tissues decreases in late larval and adult stage animals. TSP-21::GFP is also present at the surface of M lineage cells from the 1-M stage to the 16-M stage. TSP-21::GFP is enriched in the basolateral side of intestinal cells while being absent from their apical sides. In addition, while TSP-21::GFP in the M lineage cells is primarily plasma membrane localized, there is also a significant intracellular distribution of TSP-21::GFP in the M mesoblast."
Reference	"WBPaper00046810"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00023491"
Reporter_gene
Transgene	"WBTransgene00020951"
Transgene	"WBTransgene00020952"

