Pattern	"ACS-4 localizes to the surface of lipid droplets in the C.elegans intestine and skin. Robust ACS-4::GFP expression was observed throughout development in all larval stages and in adult worms. In addition to lipid droplet localization, ACS-4::GFP is expressed in a range of other tissues, including the pharynx, seam cells, dorsal and ventral nerve cords, and other cells, likely neurons, in the head and tail. Thus, ACS-4 appears to be a resident lipid droplet protein, although it may function in other tissues in C. elegans as well."
