Pattern	"The RPN-10::GFP fusion protein was expressed in multiple tissues with the strongest expression seen in the pharynx, intestine, hypodermis, and spermatheca. We also observed expression at lower levels in a broader expression pattern, including the excretory cell, body wall muscle, vulva, and somatic gonad, suggesting that the RPN-10 protein might be ubiquitously expressed."
Reference	"WBPaper00049177"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00004466"
Reporter_gene
Subcellular_localization	"The RPN-10::GFP fusion protein is visible in both the nucleus and cytoplasm."

