GO_term	"GO:0005737"
Gene	"WBGene00000386"
Pattern	"CDC-25.1 in the germline shows a very obvious gradient of abundance being at very low levels in the distal region, becoming obvious in young developing oocytes (toward the top left of the gonad shown) and increasing significantly in more mature oocytes (those toward the top right of the gonad shown). Also, although CDC-25.1 is abundant within the cytoplasm of the oocytes, it is slightly more concentrated within their nuclei. CDC-25.1 is much less abundant within the distal arm of the gonad, but extended exposures at high magnification suggest that it is present being located both outside and within the nuclei, but absent from the periphery of nuclei."
Reference	"WBPaper00035573"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00000386"

