Life_stage	"WBls:0000002"
Pattern	"sma-6 is expressed during embryonic, larval and adult stages. During the early larval stages (L1-L2), sma-6 is extensively expressed in the anterior pharyngeal and distal posterior regions of the animal. Soon afterwards, expression begins in the posterior intestinal nuclei and advances more anteriorly. Expression is seen in the pairs of intestinal nuclei as they divide. Strong expression is seen in the pharyngeal muscles of the anterior and posterior bulbs of the pharynx. Once the intestinal cell divisions are complete, one can see continued expression in the intestinal cells during L2-L3, and later disappearing in these cells. In adults, the staining pattern disappears from the midsections of the animal and persists in the pharyngeal muscles. In males, expression is seen in the tail, as predicted, but the identity of the cells is unclear. sma-6 expression is also observed in late-stage embryos."
Reference	"WBPaper00003400"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00004860"
Reporter_gene
Subcellular_localization	"intestinal nuclei"
Transgene	"WBTransgene00000281"

