Pattern	"A pitr-1 construct driven by 5.2 kb of pitr-1 upstream sequences, expressed almost ubiquitously. GFP expression was observed in the pharynx, intestine, hypodermis, body-wall muscles, nerve ring, and many other neurons, oviduct sheath cells, and spermatheca. These results suggested that pitr-1 may be expressed in the intestine at a low level, where it could directly influence yolk expression."
Reference	"WBPaper00049853"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00016739"
Reporter_gene
Transgene	"WBTransgene00032027"

