Genome_editing
Reference	"WBPaper00049906"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00019407"
Remark	"Supplementals: lect-2(dz249)[lect-2::mNG^3xFlag])II"
Reporter_gene
Subcellular_localization	"A translational fusion constructed via genome engineering was expressed diffusely from at least the gastrula stage to the 3-fold embryonic stage, at which time the fusion became more localized, possibly to cell-cell junctions. During larval and adult stages, LECT-2::mNeonGreen localized to basement membranes of hypodermal tissues and to processes of the nervous system, including commissures, sensory dendrites in the head, and lateral nerve tracts. In contrast, staining of neuronal cell bodies was less uniform. For example, neurons near the nerve ring in the head showed little or no staining, whereas cell bodies of motor neurons and some mechanosensory neu- rons (e.g., ALM) showed staining. LECT-2::mNeonGreen localized to the cell surface of a set of hypodermal cells named the seam cells and along the boundary of the lateral hypodermis. Lastly, LECT-2::mNeonGreen is seen on the basement membranes of body-wall muscles and along fibrous organelles, the desmosome-like complexes that form the physical link between body-wall muscle and hypodermis and are juxtaposed with quaternary PVD branches."
Variation	"WBVar02147193"

Expr_pattern : "Expr13007"
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0006612" Certain
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0006612" Life_stage "WBls:0000010"
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0006733" Certain
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0006733" Life_stage "WBls:0000010"
GO_term	"GO:0045179"
Gene	"WBGene00006437"
Genome_editing
Life_stage	"WBls:0000010" Anatomy_term "WBbt:0006612"
Life_stage	"WBls:0000010" Anatomy_term "WBbt:0006733"
Reference	"WBPaper00049907"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00006437"
Remark	"cp65, mrck-1(cp65[mrck-1::YPet + LoxP]) V"
Reporter_gene
Subcellular_localization	"MRCK-1::YPet was enriched in the apical cortex specifically in the gastrulating endoderm precursor cells (EPCs). A GFP-tagged strain constructed similarly showed similar localization and allowed to co-visualize MRCK-1 and an mCherry-tagged PH domain to show membranes, revealing in ventral views that MRCK-1::GFP localized to puncta across the medio-apical surfaces of EPCs as well as to apical cell-cell borders. Fluorescently tagged MRCK-1 was not enriched in the apical domain of other early embryonic interphase cells, although some enrichment could be seen in the cortex of dividing cells. In the gastrulating EPCs, enrichment was detected starting from 5 min prior to MSx division (MSx indicating the two daughters of the MS cell), and within 15 min it had reached 2-fold enrichment over cytoplasmic levels. This was significantly different from non-dividing, non-internalizing AB cells, where little enrichment over cytoplasmic levels was detected in the same time frame. Comparison of the time course of apical constriction and MRCK-1 localization shows that apical enrichment of MRCK-1::YPet is concurrent with or even precedes apical constriction and continues throughout the gastrulation movements of the EPCs."
Transgene	"WBTransgene00023458"
Variation	"WBVar02147194"

