Pattern	"RGA-7::GFP is detectable in several cells of the embryo during ventral enclosure where it accumulates as perinuclear punctate structures. RGA-7::GFP is more tubular during early elongation. During late elongation, it was mainly expressed in the dorsal and ventral hypodermal cells where it organizes itself into stripes reminiscent of filamentous actin bundles. RGA-7::GFP is also expressed in a wide range of cells in larvae and adults including the hypodermis, head and tail neurons, and spermatheca."
Reference	"WBPaper00048842"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00014051"
Reporter_gene
Transgene	"WBTransgene00023261"

