Subcellular_localization	"IFT-139::GFP was observed in ciliated sensory neurons. In the amphid neurons, the GFP signal was diffuse in dendrites and concentrated to the base of cilia. Moreover, the cilia signal was stronger than dendrite. In phasmid PHA and PHB neurons, most of the GFP signals were observed at the base of cilia and in the cilia. Phasmid dendritic signals were relatively weak compared to amphid neurons. To observe the localisation of IFT-139 at single-cell resolution, IFT-139::GFP was expressed from the PHA neuronspecic promoter, srg-13 promoter. Once again, the IFT-139::GFP signal was localised to the base of cilia and in the cilia of PHA neuron."
