Pattern	"Expression of the lst-5pro::YFP Notch activity reporter is often surprisingly asymmetric, with one of the two 2 fate VPCs sometimes exhibiting 10-fold higher fluorescence intensities than the other. P5.p and P7.p were equally likely to show stronger reporter expression. Asymmetric reporter activity was also observed during the two-cell stage of vulval development. In 9 out of 27 animals, daughters of the less bright VPC at the one-cell stage became the brighter pair of cells."
Reference	"WBPaper00050572"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00016890"
