GO_term	"GO:0005576"
Gene	"WBGene00000920"
Pattern	"The DAF-28::mCherry expression followed the reported expression pattern of pdaf-28::GFP transcriptional reporter, with fluorescent protein detected in head and tail neurons, pharynx, hypodermis, and other tissues. DAF-28::mCherry was efficiently secreted upon expression in L1 stage, as detected by its uptake by endocytic scavenger cells, coelomocytes. Interestingly, compared to the DAF-28::mCherry fusion protein, the previously described DAF-28::GFP protein was not efficiently secreted, as judged by coelomocyte fluorescence, and instead appeared to accumulate in neuronal cell bodies. This may be due to misfolding of the GFP moiety."
Reference	"WBPaper00050499"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00000920"
Reporter_gene
Subcellular_localization	"Confocal imaging showed that DAF-28::mCherry protein is predominantly found in a punctate pattern reminiscent of the secretory vesicles in mammalian cells expressing insulin or IGF, with some puncta found in a regularly spaced pattern adjacent to the ASI axons. DAF-28::mCherry was efficiently secreted upon expression in L1 stage, as detected by its uptake by endocytic scavenger cells, coelomocytes."
Transgene	"WBTransgene00024540"

Expr_pattern : "Expr13309"
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0003679" Certain
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0005451" Certain
GO_term	"GO:0030425"
GO_term	"GO:0043025"
Gene	"WBGene00000903"
Pattern	"In the wild-type background, mCherry::DAF-7 fluorescence was detected in neurons as well as in the pharyngeal muscles. In neurons, punctate fluorescence was observed in the cell bodies and in the area posterior to the ASI cell body. In contrast to DAF-28::mCherry, which was present in axons but excluded from dendrites, mCherry::DAF-7 protein was mainly detected along the dendrites of the ASI neurons. Only rare small puncta were noted in the proximal axons. Consistent with dendritic trafficking, a large accumulation of the fluorescent signal was observed surrounding the base of the ASI sensory cilia located at the distal end of the dendrite."
Reference	"WBPaper00050499"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00000903"
Reporter_gene
Transgene	"WBTransgene00024541"

