In_situ	"smFISH. RNA probes targeting tbg-1 mRNAs (Quasar 670; red) were designed using Stellaris Probe Designer (Biosearch Technologies). smFISH was performed as described previously (Osborne-Nishimura et al., 2015; Shaffer et al., 2013)."
Pattern	"tbg-1 encodes gamma-tubulin, a ubiquitous and highly conserved component of centrosomes in eukaryotic cells (Strome et al, 2001). Using smFISH we determined the localization of tbg-1 transcripts (red). tbg-1 transcripts are detected within distinct foci throughout the cytoplasm during both the first (A) and second (B) mitosis. tbg-1 transcripts are not enriched at centrosomes or either blastomere. In contrast, GFP tagged TBG-1 proteins (green signal; arrowheads) localize at centrosomes, as previously shown (Strome et al, 2001). Shown are projections from selected focal planes. Bar=10&mu;m."
Reference	"WBPaper00053033"
