Pattern	"UNC-104::GFP was expressed consistently throughout the nervous system. Distinct fluorescence was observed in neurons in the head, in the nerve ring, in the nerve cords, around the vulva, and in the tail. UNC-104::GFP was expressed during most stages of development, from late embryo to adult. Although the overall expression pattern was similar in all transgenic animals, variability was observed in the actual amount of fluorescent protein that was expressed."
