Pattern	"In predauers, Pmir-34::gfp expression was increased in amphid neurons, especially in AWC neurons. Higher expression levels were later observed in the excretory canal, seam cells and vulval precursor cells, and in ventral and dorsal nerve cord and tail neurons. Hypodermal expression appeared in day 1 dauers, and reached the highest level at the 2nd day of the dauer stage, when dauers shed their cuticle."
Reference	"WBPaper00050488"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00003262"
Reporter_gene
Transgene	"WBTransgene00024852"

Expr_pattern : "Expr13456"
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0005775" Partial
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0005775" Remark "Anterior excretory canal."
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0005812" Certain
Gene	"WBGene00000176"
Pattern	"Under normal osmolarity conditions, AQP-8::GFP localized within the excretory cell soma and throughout the entire anterior excretory canal. Within the posterior excretory canal, the signal intensity decreased from the soma toward the tail region, although the canal is fully extended throughout the whole body in adults (Khan et al., 2013; Kolotuev et al., 2013). In most animals, the signal was only visible along ~80% of the length of the posterior canal."
Reference	"WBPaper00051418"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00000176"
Reporter_gene
Transgene	"WBTransgene00024364"

