Subcellular_localization	"In the interphase of two-cell stage embryos, PLK-1::sGFP was exclusively cytoplasmic and enriched in the AB blastomere, as reported previously using PLK-1 antibodies (Budirahardja and Gonczy, 2008; Rivers et al., 2008). Concomitantly with chromosomes condensation, PLK-1::sGFP started to accumulate on chromosomes but could also be detected at the NE. The PLK-1::sGFP signal at the NE became detectable 2.5-3 min prior to NEBD. PLK-1::sGFP was similarly detected at the NE in oocytes with condensed chromosomes."
