Pattern	"In embryos with the Pmnp-1::mnp-1::gfp transgene, we first detected GFP at about 250 min after first cell division. Expression continued throughout the rest of embryonic and post embryonic development. By 350 min after first division GFP was detected in many cells whose positions suggested that they were muscle cell precursors. In 1.5-fold stage and older embryos, expression continued in putative muscle precursors. In addition, we detected GFP expression in cells whose positions were consistent with their being neuronal precursors. In young larvae through adult, Pmnp-1::mnp-1::gfp was expressed in body wall muscle cells and sometimes within neurons."
Reference	"WBPaper00050854"
