Antibody	"LIN-26 antiserum applied to hermaphrodite somatic gonad."
Antibody
Antibody_info	"WBAntibody00000122"
GO_term	"GO:0005634"
Gene	"WBGene00003012"
Life_stage	"WBls:0000003"
Life_stage	"WBls:0000023"
Pattern	"Expression in Z1 and Z4, the somatic gonad precursors, starts a few hours after these are born. Up to the formation of the somatic gonad primordium in late L2, LIN-26 protein was detected in all cells of the somatic gonad, except in the distal tip cells or dtcs (Z1.aa and Z4.pp). Staining was strongest in Z1 and Z4 and became weaker after each cell division. However, after Z1.a and Z4.p divided, LIN-26 was initially not detected in any of their daughters, but resynthesis occurred in Z1.ap and Z4.pa. During the L3 stage, expression was only detected in the anchor cell (AC) until the Pn.pxx cells were generated. After the last division round in L4 larvae, all uterine nuclei and two spermathecal-uterine junction nuclei expressed LIN-26 at very low levels."
Reference	"WBPaper00003169"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00003012"
Remark	"Expression pattern at adult stage was not described."
Subcellular_localization	"nuclei"

