Gene	"WBGene00003224"
Life_stage	"WBls:0000003"
Life_stage	"WBls:0000024"
Life_stage	"WBls:0000041"
Pattern	"In wild-type adults, MES-6 staining is most prominent in the germline, but is also detectable in intestinal nuclei. A maternal load of protein is seen in the nuclei of oocytes. In early embryos, MES-6 is present in the nuclei of all cells. As embryogenesis proceeds, staining gradually fades in somatic cells. In late embryos and L1 larvae, MES-6 remains faintly visible in a number of cell types, including the intestine, but is most prominent in Z2 and Z3, the primordial germ cells."
Reference	"WBPaper00003145"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00003224"
Subcellular_localization	"MES-6 is localized in nuclei."

