Antibody	"Polyclonal rabbit antibody that recognizes the PHA-4 carboxyl terminus."
Antibody
Antibody_info	"WBAntibody00000183"
GO_term	"GO:0005634"
Gene	"WBGene00004013"
Life_stage	"WBls:0000003"
Pattern	"PHA-4 was observed in the nuclei of cells destined to form the digestive tract. At the 4E stage, weak expression is detected in 8 MS great-granddaughters and 10 ABa descendants (ABaraaaa\/p, ABaraapa\/p, ABarapaa\/p, ABalpaaa\/p, ABalpapa\/p) that each produce pharyngeal cells, as well as nonpharyngeal cells. Faint expression was also detected in the four midgut precursors. Brighter staining is observed in 6 to 8 MS-derived and 16 to 18 ABa-derived cells after the next cell division (MSaaaa\/p, MSaapa\/p, MSpaaa\/p, MSpapa\/p). Soon thereafter, at the 8 to 12E stage, PHA-4 is first observed in the rectal precursors. Expression is maintained in all pharyngeal, midgut, and rectal cells throughout embryogenesis."
Reference	"WBPaper00003134"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00004013"
Remark	"No detailed description on postembryonic expression pattern."
Subcellular_localization	"nuclei"

