Pattern	"hlh-4 expression is not observed in any blast cells during embryonic or postembryonic development but rather is first expressed in two pairs of postmitotic cells in the precomma stage embryo, shortly after their birth. One pair is the ADL neurons and the other pair is the sisters of ADL, which die shortly after their birth by programmed cell death. Expression of hlh-4 in ADL is observed for the remainder of embryogenesis, continues during larval and adult stages, and is never observed in any other cell throughout the entire organism. The ADL-specific fosmid-based reporter expression pattern is recapitulated by a 700-bp 5' promoter fusion reporter."
Reference	"WBPaper00054218"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00001951"
Reporter_gene
Transgene	"WBTransgene00024356"
Transgene	"WBTransgene00025084"

