Pattern	"Labeled EXC-2 is located at the lumen of the excretory canal, in the corpus, posterior bulb, and pharyngeal-intestinal valve of the pharynx, as well as in the uterine seam and intestinal-rectal valve."
Reference	"WBPaper00054672"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00002056"
Reporter_gene
Subcellular_localization	"Labeled EXC-2 is located apical to canal cytoplasm, as determined via cross-sectional fluorescence intensity measurements. This result was confirmed by evaluating the subcellular location of EXC-2 relative to a known apical membrane protein, ERM-1 (Gbel et al. 2004). The results demonstrate that EXC-2 and ERM-1 show overlapping expression at the canal apical (luminal) membrane."
Variation	"WBVar02149960"

