Pattern	"IFA-4::mKate2 showed expression in several of the same locations as exc-2: the excretory canals, the pharyngeal-intestinal valve, and the intestinal-rectal valve. IFA-4 is additionally located in the spermathecal-uterine valve and cells in the vulva, including the uterine muscles and two neurons in the tail. The IFA-4 protein was also found in the gut of dauer-stage but not well-fed worms, and appeared as well in the tips of the rays and neurons of the male tail."
Reference	"WBPaper00054672"
