Pattern	"We found that in the male germline SET-17::GFP was expressed predominantly in primary spermatocytes. SET-17::GFP was first detectable at the initiation of spermatocyte differentiation in L4 and adult males. The SET-17::GFP level increased with the stage of spermatocyte progression and peaked in late-stage primary spermatocytes."
Reference	"WBPaper00054298"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00011887"
Reporter_gene
Transgene	"WBTransgene00024009"

Expr_pattern : "Expr14385"
GO_term	"GO:0000785"
Gene	"WBGene00011887"
Reference	"WBPaper00054298"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00011887"
Reporter_gene
Subcellular_localization	"Strikingly, SET-17::GFP localized to foci in the nuclei of primary spermatocytes (males). The SET-17 foci were associated with DNA, ranged from 4-14 per primary spermatocyte and increased in number with overall SET-17::GFP expression."
Transgene	"WBTransgene00024009"

Expr_pattern : "Expr14386"
GO_term	"GO:0000785"
Gene	"WBGene00011887"
Reference	"WBPaper00054298"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00011887"
Reporter_gene
Subcellular_localization	"In hermaphrodites, SET-17::GFP was similarly expressed in primary spermatocytes and localized to nuclear foci. In hermaphrodites, spermatid production occurs during the L4 stage. We also detected SET-17::GFP expression during oocyte production, even though SET-17 does not obviously function in oocytes for fertility. In hypodermal nuclei, the distribution of SET-17::GFP was pan-nuclear, suggesting that SET-17 localization to foci is related to the function of SET-17 in spermatocytes."
Transgene	"WBTransgene00024009"

