Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0006920"
Gene	"WBGene00015647"
Pattern	"GFP expression in this transgenic worm exhibited patterns similar to those observed in PC09F5.1::GFP (Expr14409). C. elegans has six symmetrical \"lips\" surrounding the mouth and the sensillar region contains various neurons (six IL1s, six IL2s, two OLLs, four OLQs, and cephalic neurons) that play general roles in mechanosensation or chemosensation. C09F5.1-GFP was localized in the six sensillar lips and in the head region in a neuron-like pattern. In addition, C09F5.1-GFP was detected in the vulval junction and the tail neuron, which was also observed in the PC09F5.1:GFP transgenic worm."
Reference	"WBPaper00053826"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00015647"
Reporter_gene

