Reporter_gene
Subcellular_localization	"In hermaphrodites, the RABS-5(WT) reporter displays vesicular or early endosome-like signals in the cell bodies colocalised with RAB-5, but is absent from the dendrite and ciliary regions, including the PCMC. However, in male-specific head (CEM) and tail (ray) ciliated neurons, an enriched pool of RABS-5 occurs at the PCMC in addition to the cell bodies. Thus, RABS-5 localises to early endosomes in ciliated neurons and displays a cell type-specific enrichment at the PCMC."
Transgene	"WBTransgene00026083"

