Subcellular_localization	"TOFU-6, PID-3, IFE-3 and ERH-2 show a characteristic perinuclear punctate localization in the germline syncytium, overlapping partially, but not fully, with the P-granule marker PGL-1. IFE-3 has a clear granular expression in the primordial germ cells in the embryo, whereas the remaining interactors show a dispersed cytoplasmic distribution across the entire early embryo. These results show that all of the identified PID-1 interactors are expressed concomitantly in early embryos, and the germline, where they are found in close proximity to P granules."
Transgene	"WBTransgene00026007"

