Pattern	"Examination of the entire germ line from mib-1(ebIs26) males by immunofluorescence revealed that GFP::MIB-1 expression occurs throughout the germ line and peaks in spermatocytes. The somatic gonad, including the distal tip cell, and spermatids all have very little\/no detectable GFP::MIB-1. Examination of sperm from dissected mib-1(ebIs26) males reveals that all detectable GFP::MIB-1 concentrates in the residual body as spermatids form and that mature sperm lack detectable GFP::MIB-1. These data indicate that MIB-1 expression occurs in germ cells and peaks during spermatocyte stages in the testes."
Reference	"WBPaper00053831"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00012933"
