Pattern	"When these minigenes were ubiquitously expressed, only a small number of body wall muscle cells at the head predominantly expressed E7a-mCherry, whereas the other tissues expressed E7b-EGFP. To determine the E7a\/E7b selections more clearly in the body wall muscle cells, these minigenes were expressed under the control of the myo-3 promoter, which is active in all body wall muscle cells (Okkema et al., 1993). These muscle-specific reporters showed that the two most anterior muscle cells in each muscle quadrant strongly expressed E7a-mCherry but only weakly expressed E7b-EGFP. The rest of the body wall muscle cells and vulval muscle cells predominantly expressed E7b-EGFP. These cells also weakly expressed E7a-mCherry."
Reference	"WBPaper00053759"
Reporter_gene
Transgene	"WBTransgene00026422"

