Subcellular_localization	"In the gonadal sheath cells, native GFP::CATP-7 localizes to large, raft-like patches on the plasma membrane, where it colocalizes with native CATP-6::mKate2. Moreover, we observe areas of the sheath cell that are positive for native CATP-6::mKate2, but not for native GFP::CATP-7. In favorable cross-section images, we were able to observe that native GFP::CATP-7 and native CATP-6::mKate2 are present on both the outer (pseudocoelom-facing) inner (germline-facing) plasma membrane surfaces of the sheath cell."
Transgene	"WBTransgene00032314"
Variation	"WBVar02150080"

