Subcellular_localization	"Retrograde cargo MIG-14-GFP expressed in coelomocytes labeled the plasma membrane, endosomes, and Golgi. We noted that MIG-14-GFP was typically unevenly distributed around the periphery of large ring-like endosomes, suggesting enrichment in endosomal subdomains. Although coelomocytes have large round endosomes, their Golgi appear as dispersed punctate structures (i.e., ministacks), as is typical of invertebrate cells. MIG-14 is likely enriched in a different subregion of the Golgi than mannosidase AMAN-2, as it usually appeared adjacent rather than directly overlapping the AMAN-2 punctae."
Transgene	"WBTransgene00023810"

