Gene	"WBGene00002081"
Life_stage	"WBls:0000002"
Pattern	"Embryos began to stain with anti-INA-1 antisera during gastrulation, with all cells expressing low levels of INA-1. In older, comma-stage embryos, there was an increased level of INA-1 in the basement membrane of the developing pharynx. Pharyngeal staining persisted in older embryos and larvae."
Reference	"WBPaper00002850"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00002081"
Remark	"Antisera from both mice and rabbits gave the same staining pattern."

