Remark	"No cellular expression pattern described."
Remark	"OGT = K04G7.3 in this article."
Subcellular_localization	"Indirect immunofluorescence of OGT using this antiserum in wild-type C. elegans embryos showed a punctate perinuclear and nuclear pattern. In embryos overexpressing the enzyme, OGT was found within the nucleus in the gut. In other regions of the embryos, the overexpressed OGT exhibited a distinct perinuclear localization. This was particularly striking in the neurons. Thus, the enzyme was found in both the nucleus and the cytoplasm, depending on the tissue overexpressing the cDNA."

