Pattern	"TIMP-1::Venus was detected on the gonadal basement membrane of the L3-stage larvae and on the basement membrane of somatic gonads and the plasma membrane of germ cells, including oocytes, of young adults. When CRI-2::Venus was expressed from the transgene tjTi86[cri-2p::cri-2::Venus], it also had a similar localization pattern. In the head region, TIMP-1::Venus and CRI-2::Venus localized to the basement and plasma membrane of the pharyngeal cells, and at the nerve ring. We then asked whether TIMP-1 and CRI-2 are secreted by examining the endocytic uptake of TIMP-1::Venus and CRI-2::Venus by coelomocytes, which are scavenger cells in the pseudocoelom. Accumulation of TIMP-1::Venus and CRI-2::Venus was observed in coelomocytes of these transgenic strains, suggesting that TIMP-1 and CRI-2 were secreted."
Reference	"WBPaper00056623"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00019476"
Reporter_gene
Transgene	"WBTransgene00025977"

