Pattern	"In adult and larval hermaphrodites, many neurons and muscle cells show expression of the reporter. These include neurons in the nerve ring, the ventral nerve cord, and the tail ganglia. Muscles expressing reporters include body wall muscles, the specialized muscles of the pharynx, and the vulva. In the male, male-specific neurons and muscle cells in the tail show the expression. Many epithelial cells in the pharynx and some vulva cells also express the reporter. No expression was observed in hypodermal cells or intestinal cells. Transgenes show similar expression pattern throughout larval development and in adult. The reporter is expressed in embryos at the comma stage and later stages."
Reference	"WBPaper00002864"
