Subcellular_localization	"We next examined the subcellular localization of DEGT-1 using a single copy transgene and found that DEGT-1 formed puncta along all levels of dendritic branches including the 4 dendrites in the PVD . The endogenous DEL-1 is present as puncta along 1-3 dendrites but not 4 dendrites, suggesting that the DEGT-1 channel's presence in 4 dendrites is required for generating Ca2+ at the terminal dendritic arbor and harsh touch-induced behavioral responses."
