Reporter_gene
Subcellular_localization	"The localization of SUPS-1::YFP and the timing of its expression suggest that SUPS-1 may be a component of the epidermal apical extracellular matrix (aECM), which forms as embryos elongate.In addition, the striated localization pattern of SUPS-1::YFP that we observe at earlier stages of its expression has been noted for other epidermal aECM proteins, such as NOAH-1 (VUONG-BRENDER et al. 2017). SUPS-1::YFP and NOAH-1::mCherry co-localized in the epidermis, suggesting that SUPS-1 is a component of, or associates with, the aECM."
Variation	"WBVar02152819"

