Subcellular_localization	"To optimize comparative imaging of all canal cIFs and their isoforms during canal lumenogenesis, ifa-4, ifb-1b, ifc-2a, and ifc-2b cDNAs were cloned behind the canal-specific sulp-5 promoter and fused to different fluorophores. All localized to expanding larval and fully expanded adult lumenal membranes adjacent to but distinct from lumenal ERM-1. Thus, all C. elegans canal cIFs and their isoforms are located at the lumen."
Transgene	"WBTransgene00027162"

