Pattern	"The immunofluorescence whole mount microscopy on embryos, larvae and adults, using the ECP-1 antibody, revealed a strong staining of the excretory cells, including the canals and the cell bodies, the pharynx, the pharyngeal-intestinal valve as well as of the intestinal-rectal valve. These results confirmed the specificity of our ECP-1 antibody and reveal that the excretory cell specific expression of ECP-1 was different from the intestinal expression of the IFC-2 protein, while the pharynx and the two intestinal valves contain both these ECP-1 and IFC-2 proteins."
Reference	"WBPaper00056896"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00002056"

