Expr_pattern : "Expr15270"
Antibody	"Commercial antibody: histone H4 (1:10,000; Millipore Sigma, 05-858)."
Antibody
GO_term	"GO:0005634"
Gene	"WBGene00001941"
Reference	"WBPaper00060516"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00001941"
Subcellular_localization	"We found H4 to be primarily localized in the nuclei of most tissues of worms, with the exception of intestinal tissue, where H4 immunostaining revealed extranuclear foci that overlapped with mitochondria. To further validate the mitochondrial localization of histone H4, we performed H4 immunofluorescence studies with C. elegans strains that express mitochondrially localized green fluorescent protein (GFP) in specific tissues. H4 immunostaining clearly showed that extranuclear H4 foci colocalized with mitochondrial GFP in the intestine, but not in the muscle cells of worms."

