Subcellular_localization	"During early meiosis I metaphase, MEI-1 was found throughout the spindle but was more abundant at the poles. Bright points were often present at the apices of the spindles. At telophase, MEI-1 staining was primarily found with the chromatin at the spindle poles. MEI-1 was also found in the polar bodies and sperm nucleus during meiosis."

