Gene	"WBGene00006751"
Genome_editing
Not_in_Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0005772"
Not_in_GO_term	"GO:0005886"
Pattern	"Similar to UNC-11 antibody staining, UNC-11::GFP expression appeared pan-neuronal and was also observed within coelomocytes. Not described by Nonet el al 1999, we observed GFP puncta in apical epithelial tissue just below the cuticle surface in both the head and in the body, an accumulation of UNC-11::GFP at the plasma membrane in the seam cells and weak staining in the vulval precursor cells (VPCs) at the interface between the VPCs and the vulval lumen. Finally, Nonet et al. described diffuse staining within the intestine whereas we did not observe detectable levels of intestinal expression, punctate or otherwise."
Reference	"WBPaper00061367"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00006751"
Reporter_gene
Variation	"WBVar02153294"

Expr_pattern : "Expr15445"
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0006796" Certain
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0007028" Certain
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0008378" Certain
GO_term	"GO:0005634"
Gene	"WBGene00010785"
Genome_editing
Pattern	"The endogenous C-terminal TOP-2::GFP is expressed in nuclei throughout the worm soma, germ line, and in developing embryos. In the germ line, TOP-2 is expressed from the mitotic zone at the distal tip to the most proximal oocyte, which is preparing for fertilization."
Reference	"WBPaper00061434"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00010785"
Reporter_gene
Variation	"WBVar02153496"

Expr_pattern : "Expr15446"
GO_term	"GO:0005654"
GO_term	"GO:0005694"
Gene	"WBGene00010785"
Genome_editing
Pattern	"The endogenous C-terminal TOP-2::GFP is expressed in nuclei throughout the worm soma, germ line, and in developing embryos. In the germ line, TOP-2 is expressed from the mitotic zone at the distal tip to the most proximal oocyte, which is preparing for fertilization."
Reference	"WBPaper00061434"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00010785"
Reporter_gene
Subcellular_localization	"In the germ line, TOP-2 is expressed from the mitotic zone at the distal tip to the most proximal oocyte, which is preparing for fertilization. During pachytene, TOP-2 is localized to the chromosomes similar to that observed in the anti-FLAG staining of TOP-2::3XFLAG germ lines. Interestingly, we observed a single TOP-2::GFP focus in pachytene nuclei. These foci are not observed with the anti-FLAG antibody staining in the TOP-2::3XFLAG germ lines. In contrast to the strictly nucleoplasmic pool of TOP-2::3XFLAG during late meiotic prophase I (diakinesis) of oocytes, we observe robust TOP-2 localization on the chromosomes of all diakinesis oocytes in addition to nucleoplasmic TOP-2::GFP."
Variation	"WBVar02153496"

Expr_pattern : "Expr15447"
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0005759" Certain
GO_term	"GO:0035869"
GO_term	"GO:0097544"
GO_term	"GO:0097730"
Gene	"WBGene00249817"
Pattern	"CEPH-41::wrmScarlet is exclusively expressed in the ciliated sensory neurons and is localized to cilia in the head (amphid) and tail (phasmid). Additionally, our co-localization analysis showed that CEPH-41 is present in the transition zone (TZ) and the proximal cilia region known as the middle segment (the microtubule doublet containing segment) in C. elegans, but not in the distal cilia region (only A-tubule containing segment)"
Reference	"WBPaper00061454"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00249817"
Reporter_gene
Transgene	"WBTransgene00032439"

