Not_in_Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0003847" Life_stage "WBls:0000002"
Pattern	"Using NeuroPAL, we confirmed sIs14542 expression in AVH, but not AVJ. We further corroborated hlh-34prom expression in AVH by observing that in the embryo, expression of otIs768 is first transiently observed in 4 cells, two of which show signs of cell death; later in embryogenesis, and then during all stages of postembryonic and adult development, expression becomes restricted to 2 cells. This is consistent with expression in the bilateral AVH neuron pair, since their two sisters cells are, unlike the sisters of the AVJ neuron pair, destined to die by apotosis (Sulston et al. 1983)."
Reference	"WBPaper00061914"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00011327"
Reporter_gene
