Gene	"WBGene00003410"
Reference	"WBPaper00048833"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00003410"
Reporter_gene
Subcellular_localization	"Immunofluorescence of embryos expressing a functional DID-2::RFP and MRP-4::GFP showed that while the staining patterns of these two proteins were fairly different, there was still extensive overlap. MRP-4::GFP stains whole membranes of compartments, while DID-2::RFP appears to stain punctate micro-domains on the same membranes or adjacent compartments. These results indicate that MRP-4 and DID-2 localize close to each other on endosomes\/lysosomes, consistent with MRP-4 protein being a substrate for DID-2\/ESCRT functions."
Transgene	"WBTransgene00032660"

