Expr_pattern : "Expr15836"
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0005753" Certain
GO_term	"GO:0005737"
GO_term	"GO:0005886"
Gene	"WBGene00003915"
Genome_editing
Life_stage	"WBls:0000003"
Life_stage	"WBls:0000023"
Life_stage	"WBls:0000041"
Pattern	"PAN-1GFP signal was detected broadly in embryos and early larvae, but decreased substantially in late larvae and adults. Two types of PAN-1GFP subcellular patterns were observed: at the cell membrane and as cytoplasmic puncta. Some prominent PAN-1GFP signal was found in seam cells, a type of epidermal cells that shows stem-cell like division during larval development. These cells were lined up in a single profile at each lateral line and embedded in syncytial epidermis. Between the seam cells and the epidermis, a ring of tight junctions formed on the apical-lateral side of the cells. By colabelling a tight-junction component DLG-1::RFP and PAN-1GFP, we observed that PAN-1 distributed at the lateral basal membrane of seam cells. PAN-1 is also localized on the cell membrane of many ventral cord neurons, including DD neurons at L1 and L2. Therefore, we observed that PAN-1 is localized on the cell membrane."
Reference	"WBPaper00061377"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00003915"
Reporter_gene
Variation	"WBVar02157206"

