Pattern	"mNG::LIN-7, LIN-2::mK2 and mNG::LIN-10 were found to bebroadly expressed in the worm. In L3 larvae, they were prominentlyexpressed in VPCs and neurons, whereas only LIN-7 and LIN-10 weredetectable in the somatic gonad primordium. In the VPCs,endogenous mNG::LIN-7 was strongly cytosolic, frequently found atpunctae, and occasionally localized to basolateral membranes. We found that LET-23::mK2 and mNG::LIN-7 overlapped at the basolateral plasma membrane in L3 larvae (from P6.p to P6.pxx). This overlap was more apparent in the differentiated vulval cells (L4)."
