Subcellular_localization	"We examined the subcellular localization of CBR-CSR-1 in embryos and found that it localizes to the nucleus, mitotic chromosomes and centrosomes from the first mitotic cell division onward. Interestingly, we also observed localization of CBR-CSR-1 to the cleavage furrow during embryonic cell divisions, a pattern that has not been described for C. elegans. However, we did not detect CBR-CSR-1 granules in the cytoplasm of embryonic germ cells."

