Subcellular_localization	"NXF-2 formed a granular structure in both the mitotic region and the meiotic region in the hermaphrodite gonads. The NXF-2 granules were mainly localized at the nuclear periphery in the mitotic region, whereas the granules were distributed uniformly throughout the whole cytoplasm in the meiotic region, although a portion of NXF-2 was also observed in the nucleus in both mitotic and meiotic germ cells. NXF-2 granules are novel structures different from P granules."
Transgene	"WBTransgene00033550"

