Life_stage	"WBls:0000003"
Life_stage	"WBls:0000023"
Pattern	"We examined the expression pattern of SNA-3::GFP throughout development. The fusion protein is found in the paternal and maternal pronuclei in one-cell embryos and expression is maintained throughout early embryogenesis, even in cells that are transcriptionally quiescent, indicating substantial parental contributions of the protein to the embryo. Somatic and germline cells express nuclear-localised SNA-3::GFP throughout postembryonic development, with expression being particularly strong in actively dividing cells, presumably reflecting the high demand for spliced leader trans-splicing."
Reference	"WBPaper00064201"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00016015"
Reporter_gene
Variation	"WBVar02158600"

