Expr_pattern : "Expr16344"
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0005772" Certain
Gene	"WBGene00022276"
Pattern	"To test this model, we built Pnlp-40::NLP- 40::mNeonGreen fusion reporter and found that nlp-40 was highly expressed in the gut beginning at an early embryonic stage and observed NLP-40 peptides in the intestine and coelomocytes, which is consistent with the previous report (Wang et al, 2013)."
Reference	"WBPaper00064204"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00022276"
Reporter_gene
Transgene	"WBTransgene00033635"

Expr_pattern : "Expr16345"
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0003961" Certain
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0003963" Certain
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0005735" Certain
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0005772" Partial
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0005772" Remark "Posterior gut."
Gene	"WBGene00000085"
Pattern	"First, we built an aex-2 transcriptional reporter Paex-2::mNeonGreen, and found that aex-2 was mainly expressed in the nervous system with some in the posterior gut, which is consistent with the previous report (Wang et al, 2013).Second, we co-expressed Paex-2::mNeonGreen with the AIY-specific marker Pttx-3::mCherry, and found that the expression of those two reporters overlapped, indicating that aex-2 is expressed in AIY interneurons."
Reference	"WBPaper00064204"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00000085"
Reporter_gene
Transgene	"WBTransgene00033636"

Expr_pattern : "Expr16346"
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0003681" Certain
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0005741" Certain
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0005772" Certain
Gene	"WBGene00002195"
Pattern	"The analysis of transgenic lines showed GFP fluorescence throughout their lifespan, which agrees well with previously published transcriptomic data (Golden et al., 2008; Gr&uuml;n et al., 2014). We found that kin-9p(2.1 kb)::GFP adults exhibited fluorescence in the pharynx, intestine, and certain cells located in the tail. While kin-9p(4.3 kb)::GFP animals exhibited a similar pattern, interestingly, no fluorescence was observed in the posterior region. It is possible that the longer fragment has certain inhibitory sequences that contribute to differences in expression."
Reference	"WBPaper00064287"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00002195"
Reporter_gene
Transgene	"WBTransgene00033638"

