Pattern	"The rml-3 transcriptional reporter showed specific rml-3 expression in the hypoderm (primarily in the seam cells, and less abundantly in the Hyp7) during larval development, starting from larval L1 through L4 and young adult (24 h post L4) stages. In dauer animals, we observed rml-3 expression predominantly in the hypodermal syncytium as seam cells were dramatically shrunk. The CRISPR GFP knock-in alleles showed identical expression patterns as the transcriptional reporter during late embryonic and larval development, albeit with lower overall fluorescence intensity of the knock- in reporter. In mature adult animals (> 48 h post L4), we observed no detectable rml-3 expression from either transcriptional or endogenous rml-3 knock-in GFP reporters."
Reference	"WBPaper00066191"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00015781"
Reporter_gene
Transgene	"WBTransgene00033868"

