Genome_editing
Life_stage	"WBls:0000038" Anatomy_term "WBbt:0005755"
Life_stage	"WBls:0000041" Anatomy_term "WBbt:0005755"
Pattern	"Endogenously tagged BLI collagens localize to puncta corresponding to cuticle struts. BLI-1::mNG fusion proteins were expressed exclusively in the late L4 epidermis and in the nascent and mature adult cuticle. Within the cuticle, BLI-1::mNG was localized to periodically repeating puncta of 0.25-0.3&mu;m in diameter in cir- cumferential rows that extended from the dorsal or ventral midlines to the lateral alae. Based on their adult-specific expression and distribution, such puncta correspond to the cuticle struts originally observed in phase contrast and in TEM16, and are consistent with localization of an extrachromosomal transgenic BLI-1::GFP reporter31,33. BLI-1::mNG animals also expressed some diffuse mNG signal in the underlying epidermis beginning in the mid-L4 stage, presumably corresponding to BLI-1::mNG in the secretory pathway. XFP knock-ins within the BLI-1 N- and C-terminal domains (ju1789 and ju1791 respectively) displayed similar localization (Fig. S2a, b); most analysis below focused on the ju1789 N-terminal mNG knock-in in 1-2 day old adults."
Reference	"WBPaper00066195"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00000251"
Reporter_gene
Variation	"WBVar02159469"

Expr_pattern : "Expr16532"
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0005755" Certain
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0007832" Certain
GO_term	"GO:0060109"
Gene	"WBGene00000252"
Genome_editing
Pattern	"Endogenously tagged BLI collagens localize to puncta corresponding to cuticle struts. To determine the localization of BLI-2 we examined a BLI-2::mNG C-terminal knock-in (syb3293). BLI-2::mNG localized to adult strut puncta in a pattern essentially indistinguishable from that of BLI- 1::mNG. Additionally BLI-2::mNG localized to the lateral alae and seam-derived cuticle and to rings surrounding sensilla. BLI-2::mNG precisely colocalized with a BLI-1::wrmScarlet marker (juEx8105) in strut puncta, but not in the lateral alae."
Reference	"WBPaper00066195"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00000252"
Reporter_gene
Variation	"WBVar02159529"

Expr_pattern : "Expr16533"
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0005755" Certain
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0007832" Certain
GO_term	"GO:0060109"
Gene	"WBGene00000256"
Genome_editing
Pattern	"Endogenously tagged BLI collagens localize to puncta corresponding to cuticle struts. A BLI-6::mNG C-terminal knock-in (ju1914) localized to strut-like puncta. Unlike BLI-1::mNG and BLI-2::mNG, which tend to be more prominent in furrow-flanking strut rows, BLI-6::mNG was most prominent in the central row of struts in each annulus, confirmed by colocalization with BLI-1::wrmScarlet. Like BLI-2::mNG, BLI- 6::mNG localized to adult alae, seen as three very bright parallel ridges as well as more diffuse localization adjacent to the alae proper. BLI- 6::mNG additionally localized to cuticle furrows, and showed diffuse localization within the cuticle, as well as to larger foci in the deeper cuticle as well as to rings surrounding sensilla and the vulva."
Reference	"WBPaper00066195"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00000256"
Reporter_gene
Variation	"WBVar02159471"

Expr_pattern : "Expr16534"
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0003844" Certain
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0003845" Certain
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0004823" Certain
Gene	"WBGene00001959"
Pattern	"We also identified a striking expression pattern for the helix-loop-helix TF hlh-15, in which expression is confined to a single neuron in the tail (DVA) and a single paired neuron in the head (AVKL\/R). A previous study generated a promoter::GFP transgene for hlh-15 and likewise reported expression in a single tail neuron and a single paired head neuron (Grove et al. 2009) but tentatively assigned the expression to the DVA and RIF neurons based on cell position and morphology. To clarify the discrepancy, we obtained the hlh- 15p::GFP transgene and crossed it with nuclear red fluorescent transgenes (H2B::mCherry) expressed in only the DVA neuron or only the AVK neuron (Wang et al. 2017). We found that the DVA mCherry marks the nucleus of the cell identified in the tail, and the AVK mCherry marks the nucleus of the paired head neurons, confirming VISTA's cell-type identification for hlh-15 gene expression."
Reference	"WBPaper00066220"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00001959"
Reporter_gene
Transgene	"WBTransgene00033875"

Expr_pattern : "Expr16535"
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0005135" Certain
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0005319" Certain
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0005829" Certain
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0006977" Certain
