Pattern	"Furthermore, animals carrying the translational reporter express a fluorescently labeled version of NHR-1 that is restricted to the nuclei of the cells in which Cel-nhr-1 is expressed. Specifically, using these localization patterns, we were able to identify the nuclei of the stomatal and pharyngeal muscle cells for which we already have seen expression signals in the transcriptional reporter line. These results confirm the presence of Cel-NHR-1 protein in exactly those cells that secrete the posterior buccal capsule. Additionally, we found Cel-NHR-1 in the nuclei of multiple nerve-ring neurons, possibly including amphid-associated neurons or glia cells."
Reference	"WBPaper00066710"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00003600"
Remark	"Reporter gene fusion not specified"
Reporter_gene

Expr_pattern : "Expr16551"
