Pattern	"Confocal microscopy analyses revealed that myt-1 was mostly expressed in body wall muscles, neurons, and intestine early during development, while it was mainly expressed in muscles and neurons in adulthood. Next, we tested myt-1 expression in 11-day-old C. elegans (counting day 0 at L4 stage) and identified an increased expression in neurons and muscles compared with younger (3-day-old) animals, confirming an age-related regulation also in C. elegans. Finally, because the initial screening was based on genes induced when nutrients are reduced, we tested whether this expression was affected by 24 hours of starvation. Consistently, GFP signal was dramatically increased by fasting, especially in body wall muscles. Thus, C. elegans replicates the mammalian tissue-pattern and age-dependent expression of MYTHO."
Reference	"WBPaper00066888"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00011344"
Reporter_gene
Transgene	"WBTransgene00033903"

