Antibody	"Freeze-crack method was used to permeabilize C. elegans embryos to explore Ce-MIF production and localization by antibody staining."
Antibody	"Polyclonal mouse antibody against Ce-MIF-3. Groups of three BALB\/c mice (68 weeks of age, females) were immunized intraperitoneally with electroeluted Ce-MIF-3 protein suspended in Imject Alum (Pierce, Rockford, IL), at a concentration of 15 mg of protein\/mouse. Mice were boosted twice with 10 mg of protein\/mouse. The anti-Ce-MIF-3 antisera were collected 735 days after the final boost."
Antibody	"Young adult worms were prepared and immunostained using a published protocol. Incubation in polyclonal mouse Ce-MIF-3 was performed overnight, worms were washed with PBS-Triton and reacted with both a Cy3-conjugated secondary goat anti-mouse IgG antibody and 1 mg\/ml 40,6-diamidino-2-phenylindole (DAPI). Samples were mounted in Vecta-shield (Vector laboratories) and examined by fluorescence microscopy and Nomarski-optics."
Antibody
