Life_stage	"WBls:0000038"
Life_stage	"WBls:0000041"
Pattern	"FEH-1 antibodies in whole-mount immunofluorescence analysis showed a largely prominent localisation of the protein in the pharynx at all stages of development, from three-fold stage embryos to adults. Barely detectable staining could be observed also in some neurons in the nerve ring and in the nerve chord and in the tail. In the pharynx the fluorescent signals start from the most terminal end of the organ and extend posteriorly to the second pharyngeal bulb and the attachment to the intestine."
Reference	"WBPaper00005169"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00001410"
Subcellular_localization	"Part of the protein appears to uniformly fill the cytoplasm of the expressing cells but an important fraction appears to associate with some sub-cellular compartment\/structure in the shape of filaments that form, at the level of the second bulb, a characteristic basket-like structure."

Expr_pattern : "Expr1866"
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0003681" Certain
