Pattern	"The expression of the ver-2::gfp fusion was restricted and found only in one pair of neurons in the head ganglia, with extending processes through the anterior of the animal. These neurons were filled with the lipophilic dye Dil and identified as ADL by the morphology of the bipolar cilia which were thinner than the wing-like shape of AWB. Indeed, coinjection of ver-2::gfp along with str-1::gfp (a pecific marker of AWB) did not show any overlap of the two markers. ver-2 was not increased when worms turned dauers."
Reference	"WBPaper00005430"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00006895"
