Pattern	"Animals with either construct expressed daf-7::GFP in the cell body of one pair of bilaterally symmetric neurons in the lateral ganglia. Based on their positions in the L1, these were identified as the two ASI neurons. GFP was consistently expressed starting in the L1, and expression became stronger in the L2. After the L2, GFP fluorescence became progressively weaker and, by adulthood, was nearly undetectable. Rarely, other cells showed weak daf-7::GFP expression. When seen, there was only one such cell, and its identity varied from animal to animal."
