Expr_pattern : "Expr2318"
Antibody	"Polyclonal peptide rabbit antibody against C. elegans UNC-59. UNC-59: actetyl-SRNDESLRTGQHKENPNYC-amide"
Antibody
Antibody_info	"WBAntibody00000329"
GO_term	"GO:0030496"
GO_term	"GO:0032154"
Gene	"WBGene00006793"
Reference	"WBPaper00004453"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00006793"
Subcellular_localization	"In UNC-59 and actin double-labeled embryos, C. elegans UNC-59 co-localized with actin. However, as cytokinesis progressed, and when the cleavage furrow constricted the midbody, UNC-59 became separated from actin. In embryos with the cleavage furrow fully ingressed, the actin ring had not reached the center of the midbody. However, at this stage UNC-59 was already appearing at the center of the midbody. Actin filaments began to aggregate at the cleavage furrow as cells underwent cytokinesis. Eventually, actin filaments concentrated at the boundary of two newly divided cells."

Expr_pattern : "Expr2319"
Antibody	"Polyclonal peptide rabbit antibody against C. elegans UNC-61. UNC-61: (acetyl-SDIEHKLQHLPPHQPC-amide)."
Antibody
Antibody_info	"WBAntibody00000330"
GO_term	"GO:0030496"
GO_term	"GO:0032154"
Gene	"WBGene00006795"
Reference	"WBPaper00004453"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00006795"
Subcellular_localization	"UNC-61 and non-muscle myosin II (NMY-II) prominently co-localize to the leading edge of the furrow. UNC-61 and NMY-II eventually also became localized to the midbody region. UNC-61 also co-localizes with actin in the cleavage furrow. Actin filaments began to aggregate at the cleavage furrow as cells underwent cytokinesis. Eventually, actin filaments concentrated at the boundary of two newly divided cells."

