Pattern	"An acr-5::gfp reporter gene containing a 4.2-kb acr-5 promoter fragment is expressed exclusively in the nervous system. Expression is initiated in the embryo and persists throughout adult life. In the ventral nerve cord of L1 larvae, acr-5::GFP expression is restricted to the embryonically derived DB motor neurons. VB motor neurons, which arise during the late L1 stage, begin to express acr-5::GFP in L2 larvae. acr-5::GFP is also expressed in other unidentified neurons in the head and tail."
Reference	"WBPaper00003757"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00000044"
Remark	"Reporter gene fusion type not specified."
Reporter_gene
Transgene	"WBTransgene00027998"

