Antibody	"Polyclonal rabbit peptide antibody against an RME-8 C-terminal fragment that contains amino acids from positions 2064 to 2270."
Antibody
Antibody_info	"WBAntibody00000393"
GO_term	"GO:0010008"
Gene	"WBGene00004378"
Life_stage	"WBls:0000035"
Life_stage	"WBls:0000038"
Life_stage	"WBls:0000041"
Pattern	"RME-8 expression in other cell types was examined by whole mount immunostaining. RME-8 is expressed in almost all cells. RME-8 was highly expressed in the lateral hypodermis, muscle, and the developing germ cells in larvae. RME-8 staining was extremely abundant in the developing uterus of L4 worms."
Pattern	"RME-8 expression was examined in dissected adult ovaries by immunofluorescence. RME-8 was highly expressed in oocytes."
Reference	"WBPaper00004810"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00004378"
Remark	"Similar expression patterns and subcellular localizations were observed by both antibody staining and RME-8::GFP reporter expression, except that RME-8::GFP was not expressed in the germline, most likely because of a general silencing of transgenes in the C. elegans germline. These observations suggest that this RME-8::GFP fusion is an accurate reporter of endogenous RME-8 expression and subcellular localization."
Reporter_gene
Subcellular_localization	"Immunofluorescence: RME-8 staining was concentrated in the cortex of oocytes beneath the plasma membrane. At high magnification, RME-8 staining was localized to punctate structures that were 0.20.4 um in diameter. RME-8 staining in the rme-8(b1023) missense mutants was diminished and mostly diffuse in the oocyte cytoplasm with little localization to cortical punctate structures . Similar mislocalization was also observed in other cell types in the mutant worms."
Subcellular_localization	"Similar expression patterns of RME-8 in somatic cells were observed with the RME-8::GFP reporter. In most cells, RME-8::GFP-labeled small puncta with sizes similar to the puncta stained with RME-8 antibodies. In live coelomocytes, RME-8::GFP labeled the limiting membranes of larger vesicles, with diameters ranging from 0.5 to 4.0 um. By serial thin-section confocal microscopy, these vesicles appeared to be round regardless of their sizes, but after fixation, these RME-8::GFP-labeled vesicles appeared smaller, as if they had collapsed."
Subcellular_localization	"Whole mount immunostaining: in all the cells examined, RME-8 staining was localized to cytoplasmic punctate structures similar to those seen in the oocytes."
Transgene	"WBTransgene00000153"

