Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00006914"
Subcellular_localization	"VHA-5 was detectable in a dot-like compartment in every embryonic cell. The compartment was found exclusively around the nucleus and observed during embryogenesis. A cup-shaped structure was often observed around nuclei instead of the dot-like compartment. On the other hand, VHA-5 expression changed dramatically at the larval stage and became dominant in an H-shaped excretory cell, consistent with the results for transgenic worms carrying the vha-5::GFP fusion gene. See Expr2403 for vha-5 GFP analysis."

Expr_pattern : "Expr2407"
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0005767" Certain
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0005772" Certain
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0006873" Certain
Antibody	"Polyconal rabbit antibody. A 350-bp (Glu-69 to Leu-180 of VHA-6) cDNA fragment was inserted into pGEX5X-1(Amersham Pharmacia Biotech). The recombinant proteins expressed in Escherichia coli were used to immunize rabbits, and the antisera were affinity-purified using the same recombinant protein."
Antibody
Antibody_info	"WBAntibody00000406"
GO_term	"GO:0016471"
GO_term	"GO:0045177"
Gene	"WBGene00006915"
Life_stage	"WBls:0000003"
Life_stage	"WBls:0000024"
Life_stage	"WBls:0000027"
Life_stage	"WBls:0000035"
Life_stage	"WBls:0000038"
Life_stage	"WBls:0000041"
Pattern	"After the comma stage in embryos, expression of VHA-6 changed. In 2-fold embryos, VHA-6 was limited to the intestine. Such intestinal expression was also observed in larvae and adults. The C. elegans intestine comprises a tube formed from 20 cells with microvilli on their apical surface. Furthermore, VHA-6 was clearly found at the junction between the pharynx and the intestine."
Pattern	"VHA-6 was preferentially localized in dot-like structures in P2 cells of 4-cell stage embryos. Only single cells continued to express VHA-6 during further development. After the cleavage stage (~300 cells), when intestinal cells appear, VHA-6 was detected in two distinct cell types. These two cell types were aligned on both lateral sides at the comma stage. The expression pattern of VHA-6 was similar to the cell-specific distribution of P granules, which are passed onto a germ line cell lineage from P2 cells."
Reference	"WBPaper00004842"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00006915"
Subcellular_localization	"VHA-6 was preferentially localized in dot-like structures in P2 cells of 4-cell stage embryos. VHA-6 was clearly detectable on the apical surface of intestinal cells, forming two lines along the worm body."

