Expr_pattern : "Expr2466"
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0005733" Certain
Antibody	"Rabbit WSP-1 polyclonal antiserum was raised against amino acids 475 to 598, corresponding to the VCA region of WSP-1. The antigen was first expressed as a GST fusion protein. The GST moiety was removed by thrombin digestion, and the resulting antigen was injected into rabbits. Antiserum was purified with CNBr-sepharose beads covalently coupled to the antigen."
Antibody
Antibody_info	"WBAntibody00000620"
GO_term	"GO:0030864"
Gene	"WBGene00006957"
Life_stage	"WBls:0000003"
Reference	"WBPaper00005843"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00006957"
Remark	"In wsp-1(RNAi) embryos, WSP-1 protein levels were reduced and localization at boundaries was diminished. Reduction of the protein level of WSP-1 was observed in almost all the RNAi-treated embryos, including those that would undergo normal embryogenesis. Anti-actin staining of wsp-1(RNAi) embryos did not significantly alter the actin skeleton compared to wild-type embryos."
Subcellular_localization	"During early embryogenesis, WSP-1 colocalized with actin at the blastomere boundary. During ventral enclosure, WSP-1 colocalized with actin at the periphery of cells, including in hypodermal cells migrating to the ventral side."

