Pattern	"Expression was first observed in the developing embryo at the 1.5- to 2-fold stage, also observed in larvae and adults. Expression observed in body wall muscle, anal depressor muscle and vulval muscles."
Reference	"WBPaper00005938"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00006827"
Remark	"Five independent lines in a wild-type background showed the same pattern of expression, although the level of expression varied somewhat between transgenic lines. Significantly, the same UNC-98::GFP was used to create two independent lines in an unc-98(su130) background, and both lines are fully rescued with respect to the muscle phenotype. In addition, the UNC-98::GFP showed that same pattern of expression and intracellular localization in both wild-type and unc-98(su130) backgrounds."
Reporter_gene
Subcellular_localization	"Expression was first observed in the developing embryo at the 1.5- to 2-fold stage, in which the UNC-98-GFP protein seemed localized to filamentous tracts, which generally follow myosin heavy chain A antibody staining, and therefore are interpreted to be located in myofibrils. Additionally, expression is seen in undefined puncta located along the filamentous tracts. In larvae and adults, expression was seen in body wall muscle, and in addition, anal depressor muscle and vulval muscles. Within adult body wall muscle, the UNC-98-GFP fusion localizes to dense bodies and M-lines. Within these muscle cells, prominent localization of the UNC-98-GFP in the nucleus was also seen. The UNC-98-GFP colocalizes with the DNA-binding dye DAPI. The signal is excluded from what seems to be the nucleolus and the UNC-98-GFP signal is discontinuous. This nuclear localization is consistent with the presence of the NLS sequences noted above. During development, the nuclear localization of UNC-98::GFP begins at the late L2 to early L3 larval stages."
Transgene	"WBTransgene00028088"

Expr_pattern : "Expr2578"
Antibody	"Affinity purified rabbit polyclonal antibodies against recombinant full-length UNC-98 protein."
Antibody
Antibody_info	"WBAntibody00000647"
GO_term	"GO:0005634"
GO_term	"GO:0031430"
Gene	"WBGene00006827"
Reference	"WBPaper00005938"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00006827"
Remark	"EU131 staining was undetectable in the muscle of each of the unc-98 mutants, consistent with the absence of the 37-kDa polypeptide on Western blots, and thus demonstrating the specificity of the antibodies for UNC-98 protein."
Subcellular_localization	"In wild-type muscle fixed with methanol and paraformaldehyde on whole worms, or alternatively, ethanol or methanol on worm frozen sections, anti-UNC-98 staining was only found at the M-line; no staining was observed at the dense bodies or in nuclei. However, when frozen sections were fixed with n-heptane, staining of M-lines and, in addition, the muscle cell nuclei was observed. Thus, it would seem that there is indeed UNC-98 in the nucleus, but the epitopes detected by these antibodies are inactivated by the usual fixatives."
Subcellular_localization	"UNC-98 antibodies were used to stain animals genotypically unc-98(su130) that were rescued with a transgenic array carrying the 8.1-kb unc-98rescuing fragment and rol-6 marker DNA. Because extrachromosomal arrays contain multiple expressed copies of an introduced gene, these unc-98-rescued animals are likely to express higher than wildtype levels of UNC-98. In these unc-98-rescued animals, anti-UNC-98 antibodies localize to all three structures labeled with UNC-98-GFP: M-lines, nuclei, and dense bodies."
Subcellular_localization	"When used against wild-type embryos, these antibodies stain filamentous structures, presumably myofibrils, as early as the 1.5- to 2-fold stage. In wild-type adult animals fixed with methanol and paraformaldehyde, these antibodies stain the M-line region, colocalizing with UNC-89, a previously described component of the M-line region."

