Expr_pattern : "Expr2680"
Antibody	"Rabbit polyclonal antibody against SYP-2. Rabbit a-SYP-2 C-terminal polyclonal antibodies were generated using a peptide antigen corresponding to the final 20 amino acid residues of SYP-2. The a-SYP-2 C-terminal antibody does not detect SYP-2 either on chromosomes in situ or on Westerns in either syp-2(me19) or syp-2(ok307) mutants, indicating that the antibody is specific to SYP-2."
Antibody
Antibody_info	"WBAntibody00000673"
GO_term	"GO:0000795"
GO_term	"GO:0005634"
Gene	"WBGene00006376"
Reference	"WBPaper00006086"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00006376"
Subcellular_localization	"The timing of SYP-2 localization with chromosomes corresponds well with the timing of assembly and disassembly of the synaptonemal complex. The first few nuclei entering meiotic prophase contain a single bright focus of SYP-2 and are followed by nuclei that contain two or more foci. Later within the transition zone, short stretches of SYP-2 are observed instead of foci. Upon entrance into and throughout the pachytene stage, SYP-2 localizes in a continuous fashion at the interface between paired and aligned homologous chromosomes."

Expr_pattern : "Expr2681"
Antibody	"Polyclonal rabbit antibody against TAC-1. Full-length tac-1 cDNA was subcloned into pGEX-6P. GST-TAC-1 fusion protein was produced, purified, and digested with PreScission protease. TAC-1 was then injected into a rabbit according to standard procedures."
Antibody
Antibody_info	"WBAntibody00000668"
GO_term	"GO:0000922"
GO_term	"GO:0005737"
GO_term	"GO:0005813"
GO_term	"GO:0005819"
Gene	"WBGene00006381"
Reference	"WBPaper00006059"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00006381"
Subcellular_localization	"TAC-1 is slightly enriched at spindle poles during the meiotic division. A more significant enrichment of TAC-1 was observed at centrosomes in one-cell-stage embryos during prophase; the intensity of this centrosomal signal increases further throughout mitosis, and culminates in anaphase. During metaphase, TAC-1 is also weakly enriched on the spindle, particularly in the vicinity of chromosomes. TAC-1 is present in the cytoplasm of early embryos throughout the cell cycle. Both centrosomal and cytoplasmic signals are essentially absent in tac-1(RNAi) embryos; the absence of these signals confirms that they correspond to bona fide TAC-1 distribution."

Expr_pattern : "Expr2682"
Antibody	"Polyclonal rabbit antibody against recombinant ZYG-9 protein. Fusion protein containing the carboxy-terminal 462 amino acids of the ZYG-9 protein was prepared for polyclonal antibody production. A fragment containing 1,385 base pairs from the 3' end of the zyg-9 cDNA was cloned into the expression vector QE30 (QIAGEN, Inc., Santa Clarita, CA). ZYG-96HIS fusion proteins were expressed in bacteria, inclusion bodies were isolated, and then the expected 51-kD protein was purified by SDS-PAGE followed by electroelution and dialysis. Rabbit polyclonal antibodies were generated at the Cornell Research Animal Resources Facility (Ithaca, NY). ZYG-9specific antibodies were purified from crude serum by column chromatography using ZYG-9 fusion protein coupled to CNBr-activated Sepharose 6MB beads (Pharmacia Biotech., Inc., Piscataway, NJ)."
Antibody
Antibody_info	"WBAntibody00000179"
GO_term	"GO:0000922"
GO_term	"GO:0005737"
GO_term	"GO:0005813"
Gene	"WBGene00006994"
Reference	"WBPaper00003099"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00006994"
Subcellular_localization	"ZYG-9 exhibits a dynamic cell cycle-dependent distribution pattern. The protein localizes to the meiotic spindle and spindle poles and to the mitotic centrosomes. In metaphase and early anaphase stages, ZYG-9 can be detected over the central mitotic spindle region as well. During interphase, ZYG-9 protein is distributed throughout the cytoplasm. Specificity of this staining pattern was confirmed by its absence in embryos homozygous for any of three strong zyg-9 alleles that lacked the 155-kD protein."

Expr_pattern : "Expr2683"
Antibody	"Polyclonal rabbit antibody against TAC-1 recombinant protein. The full-length TAC-1 cDNA was amplified by PCR from EST yk96g12 and was cloned in the pDONR201 vector (Gateway Technology, Invitrogen) to generate entry clone pJA90. A construct for expressing a GST:TAC-1 fusion was generated by recombining pJA90 with pDEST15 to generate pJA91, and another for expressing MBP:TAC-1 was produced by recombining pJA90 with a pmalC2-Gateway vector to generate pJA92. The GST:TAC-1 fusion protein was injected into rabbits for antibody production, and antibodies were affinity purified by using a column coupled to MBP:TAC-1."
Antibody
Antibody_info	"WBAntibody00000669"
GO_term	"GO:0000922"
GO_term	"GO:0005813"
GO_term	"GO:0005819"
Gene	"WBGene00006381"
Reference	"WBPaper00006060"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00006381"
Subcellular_localization	"TAC-1 is first associated with the meiotic spindle and is enriched at the spindle poles. As the sperm aster grows, TAC-1 is recruited to the centrosomes, where it accumulates as they mature, reaching a peak at metaphase. At telophase, centrosomal TAC-1 association becomes weaker."

Expr_pattern : "Expr2684"
GO_term	"GO:0005813"
GO_term	"GO:0005818"
GO_term	"GO:0051233"
Gene	"WBGene00006381"
Reference	"WBPaper00006060"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00006381"
Reporter_gene
Subcellular_localization	"GFP:TAC-1 is localized to the centrosomes before pro-nuclear migration and becomes highly concentrated there, reaching a peak at metaphase. During anaphase, GFP:TAC-1 starts to disappear from the center of the aster. By the end of telophase, two foci of GFP:TAC-1, which are probably associated with the newly duplicated centrosome, are observed in the center of the \"old\" ring of GFP:TAC-1. During interphase, centrosomal GFP:TAC-1 reaccumulates until the next mitosis. GFP:TAC-1 is also weakly associated with the central spindle around the chromosomes at metaphase."
Transgene	"WBTransgene00005047"

