Antibody	"Polyclonal rabbit peptide antibody. A synthetic peptide CAGGSGVDSSKAVAN corresponding to residues 395-408 of UNC-78 plus additional cysteine at the N terminus was synthesized to raise rabbit antisera."
Antibody
Antibody_info	"WBAntibody00000674"
GO_term	"GO:0042643"
Gene	"WBGene00006810"
Life_stage	"WBls:0000018"
Life_stage	"WBls:0000019"
Life_stage	"WBls:0000020"
Life_stage	"WBls:0000021"
Pattern	"Immunolocalization of UNC-78 revealed that UNC-78 is expressed in a tissue-specific manner. In embryos, faint staining of UNC-78 was first detected in a subset of cells at the 1.5-fold stage (~350 minutes after the first cell division). In the later embryonic stages, UNC-78 was expressed in the body wall muscle and also more strongly in the pharynx. In adults, UNC-78 was expressed in the body wall muscle, pharynx and spermatheca."
Reference	"WBPaper00006108"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00006810"
Remark	"Staining of unc-78 null mutants with anti-UNC-78 antibody did not yield these patterns, indicating that striated staining is specific for reactivity with UNC-78."
Subcellular_localization	"In 1.5-fold embryos: The UNC-78-positive regions were adjacent to the nascent myofibrils in body wall muscle where the muscle-specific myosin heavy chain myoA was localized, suggesting that UNC-78 is localized in the diffuse cytoplasm of the body wall muscle cells."
Subcellular_localization	"In later embryos, in the pharynx and spermatheca, subcellular localization of UNC-78 was not clear owing to poor penetration of the antibody into these tissues. In the body wall muscle, UNC-78 was localized in a striated pattern that was co-localized with actin but not with the myosin heavy chain myoA. However, since the striation of UNC-78 was not as sharp as that of actin, it was difficult to determine precise location of UNC-78 within the thin filaments."

