Life_stage	"WBls:0000024"
Life_stage	"WBls:0000057"
Pattern	"Expressed in early embryos. The staining in the embryos was specific because it was largely reduced in syn-4(RNAi) embryos compared with wild-type embryos. In L1-stage larvae, prominent staining was detected in two rows of cells, which appeared to be the cuticle-secreting seam cells. In the adult hermaphrodite, Syn-4 was largely confined to the gonad."
Reference	"WBPaper00003608"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00006374"
Reporter_gene
Subcellular_localization	"An identical pattern of gonadal staining was observed in an adult expressing a GFP::Syn-4 fusion construct."
Subcellular_localization	"Syn-4 was present in the outer membrane of early embryos. During cytokinesis, Syn-4 staining was observed in furrows that had just begun to ingress and as the membrane invaginated, the extent of Syn-4 staining expanded. Syn-4 remained associated with the membranes that separate blastomeres. The punctate staining pattern observed in the cytoplasm of early embryos probably reflects vesicular structures, which were often enriched around the forming nuclei. In the adult hermaphrodite, Syn-4 was largely confined to the gonad, where it localized to the incomplete membranous structures that separate the germ cell nuclei."
Transgene	"WBTransgene00028152"

