Pattern	"As shown in embryos reacted with a polyclonal mouse antiserum against the N-terminal 325 amino acids of Ce-RCQ-5, RCQ-5 protein was present in nuclei throughout embryogenesis, which differed from the lower mRNA level at the late embryonic stage. RCQ-5 protein was also present in nuclei of all the germ cells, oocytes, and intestinal cells."
Reference	"WBPaper00006268"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00004322"
Subcellular_localization	"Expressed in nuclei. Disappearance of nuclear immunostaining in an embryo upon RNAi targeted to Ce-rcq-5 supported specificity of the antibody."

Expr_pattern : "Expr2822"
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0004017" Certain
GO_term	"GO:0005634"
Gene	"WBGene00004322"
Life_stage	"WBls:0000003"
