Pattern	"Anti-IFB-1 was previously reported to stain several non-epidermal cell types. Anti-IFB-1 staining in these cells was confirmed; however, in addition, consistent anti-IFB-1 staining was observed in epidermal attachment structures. The expression patterns of the GFP-tagged IFB-1 transgenes support the conclusion that this anti-IFB-1 staining in epidermal cells is specific."
Reference	"WBPaper00006428"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00002053"
Remark	"No detailed description on cellular expression patterns in other tissue."
Subcellular_localization	"Expressed in epidermal attachment structures."

