Pattern	"The transgenic animals started to express the construct during late embryogenesis. GFP expression was not found in early embryogenesis. A late embryo showed diffuse expression. In early larvae, a faint and diffuse staining was observed in all tissues. The C05D11.3::GFP continued to be expressed in most cells of the nervous system, at all larval stages and in adult animals: the ventral nerve cord as well as dorsal and lateral cords. And it is expressed in the pharynx. Larval stages showed strong expression, in particular non-neuronal cells. Furthermore, an oval of fluorescence in the middle of the L4 worm suggested that C05D11.3 was expressed in the vulva. After the L4 stage, C05D11.3::GFP expression was seen in the vulva in all life. A more detailed analysis of this expression indicate that C05D11.3 is highly expressed in the nervous system and vulva."
Reference	"WBPaper00006406"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00006515"
Reporter_gene
Subcellular_localization	"C05D11.3::GFP is partly co-localized with DAPI, suggesting that C05D11.3 is localized both in the nucleus and the cytoplasm."
Transgene	"WBTransgene00028228"

