Pattern	"In transgenic animals, sgk-1::gfp expression starts in late embryos just before hatching. At postembryonic stages, sgk-1::gfp is expressed in sensory (e.g., ASK, ADL, ASI) and many other neurons. In the tail, sgk-1::gfp is expressed in the sensory neurons PHA and PHB and in the interneurons LUA (identified by costaining with DiI). sgk-1::gfp expression was also observed in the motor neurons of the ventral nerve cord and in the intestine."
Reference	"WBPaper00013413"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00004789"
Reporter_gene
Subcellular_localization	"In neurons, SGK-1::GFP is localized both in the cytoplasm and in the nucleus, whereas in the intestine it is exclusively cytoplasmic."
Transgene	"WBTransgene00000182"

