Pattern	"In late embryos (after the comma stage) matefin staining decreased in all somatic cells but intensified in the nuclear envelopes of the two primordial germ cells, Z2 and Z3. The identity of Z2 and Z3 cells was verified by double labeling with antibodies against PGL-1, which is specific to germ cells. Throughout larva stages L1-L4 and in adults, matefin was present only in germ cells. Matefin signal declined during spermatogenesis and was undetectable in sperm."
Reference	"WBPaper00006526"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00006311"
Subcellular_localization	"Matefin was detected at the nuclear envelope of all early embryonic cells."

