Pattern	"Expression was prominent in the ALA neuron in the dorsal ganglion of the pharyngeal nerve ring, the hermaphrodite-specific vulval motoneurons HSN, VC4 and VC5, the neuroendocrine-like uv1 cells, the tail neuron pair PHC, was also present in the ventral cord neurons VC1, VC2, VC3, VC6, and was somewhat variable in a few amphid neurons."
Reference	"WBPaper00013484"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00002048"
Reporter_gene
Subcellular_localization	"Cytoplasmic GFP fluorescence was high in cell bodies and extended into the nerve processes in a distinct punctate pattern. The subcellular distribution of IDA-1::GFP was similar to that of IDA-1 as observed by immunofluorescence microscopy of wild-type animals (see Expr2969), as best observed in the ALA lateral process and PHC."
Transgene	"WBTransgene00000648"
Transgene	"WBTransgene00000649"

