Pattern	"For din-1L, 8 kb of the din-1 upstream region was placed before gfp followed by din-1LB cDNA. Extrachromosomal arrays dhEx191 and dhEx194 were expressed in the nuclei of most cells from embryo to adult, as well as in dauer larvae. din-1L expressed more strongly in embryo and L1 larvae than din-1S, consistent with an earlier role."
Pattern	"din-1S::gfp localized to the nuclei of most cell types. Detected in hypodermis, seam, intestine, and somatic gonad including the distal tip cells, din-1S was also expressed in neurons, vulval precursors, body wall muscle, and pharynx, all tissues with heterochronic phenotypes or remodeled during dauer. Expression was first detected in a few nuclei by the comma stage of embryogenesis. By hatch, din-1S was widely expressed, albeit weakly. Overall expression in most tissues was detected at various levels into adult and in dauer larvae. Interestingly, in late L1 and L2 larvae din-1S was often (75%, n = 16) highly expressed in the XXX cells, specialized neuroendocrine cells proposed to be a site of synthesis for the daf-9-produced hormone."
Reference	"WBPaper00024451"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00008549"
Reporter_gene
Subcellular_localization	"Expressed in nuclei."
Transgene	"WBTransgene00028312"

