Subcellular_localization	"In wild-type animals, no GPA-6 immunoreactivity could be detected. However, in animals overexpressing GPA-6, the dendrites, cell bodies, and axons of four pairs of amphid neurons, but not the cilia, showed staining. The positions of the cell bodies and colocalization experiments suggested that these cells are AWA, AWB, ADL, and ASH. No staining was observed in the ASI cells. The two pairs of phasmid neurons, PHA and PHB, and a third unidentified cell, posterior to these neurons, were also visible."

