Gene	"WBGene00003047"
Reference	"WBPaper00024358"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00003047"
Subcellular_localization	"LIS-1 is present throughout the cytoplasm, but is also enriched in discrete subcellular locations. In early one-cell-stage embryos, LIS-1 is typically detected within pronuclei during late prophase, before NEBD would be apparent by DIC microscopy. In favourable specimens, LIS-1 can also be detected at the nuclear periphery during late prophase (two-cell-stage embryo) as well as in the vicinity of chromosomes during prometaphase. LIS-1 is depleted from the centres of microtubule asters during prometaphase, whereas it is enriched throughout the spindle during metaphase and early anaphase. During late anaphase and telophase, LIS-1 staining diminishes on the spindle but becomes enriched in the vicinity of the microtubule asters. Moreover, LIS-1 enrichment becomes apparent at the cell cortex at this stage. The discrete subcellular distributions of LIS-1 are typically more readily detectable in subsequent cell cycles. This is especially true of the nuclear enrichment in prophase, of the spindle enrichment in metaphase and of the cortical localization. Whereas foci of LIS-1 colocalize with the plus end of some astral microtubules, this is not always the case, and many LIS-1 foci are found throughout the microtubule lattice. Therefore, C. elegans LIS-1 is not detected strictly at the plus end of microtubules."

Expr_pattern : "Expr3078"
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0003732" Certain
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0005772" Certain
Gene	"WBGene00003473"
Pattern	"The major location of the cadmium inducible metallothionein expression was strictly confined to the intestine, mtl-1 was constituently expressed, even in the absence of cadmium, in the second pharyngeal bulb."
Reference	"WBPaper00024351"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00003473"
Remark	"The GFP signal could be turned on by exposing nematodes to metals. The overall response characteristics mirrored the data obtained from the semi-quantitative PCR, namely the minimum response concentration was 2.5 M cadmium over a 24 hour exposure period and, as before, copper and zinc were poor inducers. Short-term exposures of one hour required a cadmium concentration in excess of 20 M to initiate a strong positive GFP signal. Although there was no observable isoform specific divergence in signal intensity, dose or time response, the cellular localisation differed to some extent."
Reporter_gene
Transgene	"WBTransgene00028340"

