Pattern	"Bright fluorescence was observed in the Hyp5 hypodermal cell at the anterior end of the larvae as well as at other attachment points of the cuticle at the anterior end of larvae, in the arcade cells in the mouth, the anterior pharynx and the amphid socket cells, and in the rectal epithelial cells at the posterior end of the larvae. Bright fluorescence was also observed in the hypodermal cells of each larval stage. Expression was not seen in the seam cells of L1 through L3 larvae; however, the seam cells of the L4 larvae strongly expressed nas-37::GFP. The L4 stage is when the seam cells terminally differentiate and fuse with the hypodermal syncytium. The expression in the hypodermis and seam cells disappeared in adult worms after a few hours. However, expression continued in the vulval epithelial cells and the rectal epithelial cells in the adult."
Reference	"WBPaper00024579"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00003553"
Reporter_gene
Transgene	"WBTransgene00028375"

Expr_pattern : "Expr3125"
