Pattern	"GFP expression was detected in four cells near the nerve ring as well as in two dendrites that extend toward the mouth displaying a pattern similar to that seen in C. elegans when amphid neurons are stained. The GFP shows a web-like pattern that seems to extend away from each of the cells. Weak GFP expression can also be seen in cells of developing embryos. These cells were identified as sheath cells of the cephalic sensilla. Expression in these cells is detected at all developmental stages and in both males and hermaphrodites."
Reference	"WBPaper00026651"
