Expr_pattern : "Expr333"
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0003679" Certain
Antibody	"Antisera against a RAB-3 fusion protein produced in E. coli"
Antibody
Antibody_info	"WBAntibody00000151"
Gene	"WBGene00004267"
Pattern	"~all neurons. Immunoreactivity was detected in the synaptic-rich regions of the nervous system in a pattern similar to the distribution of the C. elegans synaptic vesicle membrane protein synaptotagmin. Specifically, the nerve ring, ventral nerve cord, and dorsal nerve cord showed the highest immunoreactivity. rab-3 expression also was observed in the pharyngeal nervous system. Detectable levels of RAB-3 were rarely observed in neuronal cell bodies, dendrites of sensory neurons, or the commissural tracts of motor neurons. In contrast to synaptotagmin, RAB-3 protein was not observed at significant levels in the gonadal uv1 neurosecretory cells. Additionally, RAB-3 was not observed in muscle, hypodermis, or intestinal tissue. Analysis of transgenic animals carrying the rab-3::lacZ reporter construct pMG122 confirmed that the gene is expressed in most, if not all, neurons but is not expressed in other tissues."
Reference	"WBPaper00002918"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00004267"
Remark	"Data modified according to Shawn Lockery's expression pattern curations."

