GO_term	"GO:0005818"
GO_term	"GO:0005819"
GO_term	"GO:0005938"
Gene	"WBGene00004367"
Reference	"WBPaper00024543"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00004367"
Remark	"With the exception of the staining at the nuclear envelope and around the chromatin, the RIC-8 staining is reduced in ric-8(md1909);ric-8(RNAi) but not completely abolished, consistent with a partial RNAi effect. All staining patterns are absent in a preadsorbed antibody preparation, confirming the specificity of the antibodies. Two additional lines of evidence suggest that the nuclear envelope staining is specific. This localization was also observed with a different antibody generated by Miller and Rand, and GFP::RIC-8 embryos show the same localization pattern."
Reporter_gene
Subcellular_localization	"The subcellular localization of RIC-8 is very similar to the localization of GOA-1, for example at the cortex and on the asters of the mitotic spindle. In addition, RIC-8 was found to be localized on the central spindle, as GPR-1\/2, at the nuclear envelope and around the chromatin."
Transgene	"WBTransgene00000338"

