Pattern	"At the L4 stage, SMO-1::GFP marker was expressed in each of the 64 uterine cells, the somatic spermathecal cells, the sheath cells that cover the gonadal arms, the hypodermis, and seam cells. The two DTCs of the somatic gonad also expressed the transgene. At the early L3 stage, expression was detected in the six vulval precurcor cells (VPCs), and at the L4 stage SMO-1::GFP was found in all 22 vulval nuclei, as well as in the gonadal anchor cell (AC). The lack of germ cell expression could be attributed to germ-line silencing. Expression in embryos was detected as early as the gastrulation stage."
Reference	"WBPaper00024467"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00004888"
