GO_term	"GO:0031594"
GO_term	"GO:0043196"
Gene	"WBGene00002977"
Reference	"WBPaper00024414"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00002977"
Remark	"LEV-10A or LEV-10B were expressed under the control of the muscle-specific promoter myo-3 in lev-10(kr26) animals. Both proteins rescued behavioural defects and UNC-29 synaptic clustering when expressed in muscle. Genetic mosaic analysis confirmed that LEV-10 is required cell autonomously in postsynaptic muscle cells for AChR clustering at NMJs."
Subcellular_localization	"In wild-type animals, LEV-10 is concentrated at cholinergic NMJs. Double labelling experiments with an antibody against the vesicular acetylcholine transporter UNC-17 demonstrated that 93 plusminus 3% of LEV-10 puncta were associated with cholinergic varicosities (mean plusminus SEM, 104 puncta counted in seven worms). However, three-dimensional analysis of confocal image stacks revealed that LEV-10 staining was juxtaposed to, but did not overlap, UNC-17 distribution."

