Gene	"WBGene00005020"
Life_stage	"WBls:0000003"
Reference	"WBPaper00026630"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00005020"
Remark	"To determine whether the antibody was against the Gal-T2 protein and not the recombinant tags or putative N- or O-glycan side chains, Western blot analysis against recombinant and deglycosylated Gal-T2 protein preparations were used. ELISA and Western blot analysis showed that the antibody recognized a recombinant Gal-T2 (31 to 330-aa) protein preparation, lacking the purification tags."
Subcellular_localization	"The anti-Gal-T2 scFv showed a strong immunofluorescence signal in all cells of early and late embryo specimens, revealing numerous punctate organelles surrounding the nucleus. Nuclei were always devoid of fluorescence and the pattern of anti-Gal-T2 scFv antibody fluorescence is similar to that seen with other examples of worm Golgi proteins."

