Life_stage	"WBls:0000038"
Life_stage	"WBls:0000041"
Northern
Pattern	"bec-1 mRNA was present in all developmental stages; however, the strongest expression was observed during embryogenesis. The increased level of bec-1 mRNA in adults presumably results from the gonad and\/or embryos, since glp-1 mutants, which do not contain germ cells, showed low steady-state levels of bec-1 transcript"
Reference	"WBPaper00026705"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00000247"

Expr_pattern : "Expr3647"
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0005175" Certain
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0005772" Certain
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0005829" Certain
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0006748" Certain
GO_term	"GO:0005634"
GO_term	"GO:0005737"
GO_term	"GO:0031410"
Gene	"WBGene00000247"
Life_stage	"WBls:0000003"
Life_stage	"WBls:0000024"
Life_stage	"WBls:0000027"
Life_stage	"WBls:0000035"
Life_stage	"WBls:0000038"
Life_stage	"WBls:0000041"
Pattern	"BEC-1::GFP was ubiquitously expressed throughout development. Its expression level appeared to be most intense in differentiating organs, such as the presumptive ventral nerve cord, the intestine, the developing vulva, and the somatic gonad. The distribution of BEC-1::GFP corresponded to the expression pattern of a transcriptional bec-1::gfp fusion construct reported earlier [see Expr2694]."
Reference	"WBPaper00026705"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00000247"
Reporter_gene
Subcellular_localization	"The BEC-1::GFP fusion protein was located in the cytoplasm of many cell types and often accumulated in vesicle-like structures. Some expression was also observed in the nucleus."
Transgene	"WBTransgene00028787"

Expr_pattern : "Expr3648"
GO_term	"GO:0000932"
Gene	"WBGene00003582"
Gene	"WBGene00015547"
Gene	"WBGene00021929"
Reference	"WBPaper00026707"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00003582"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00015547"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00021929"
Reporter_gene
Subcellular_localization	"The punctate cytoplasmic pattern of AIN-1::GFP resembles that of the P bodies. By using an anti-DCAP-2 antibody, DCAP-2 has been localized to cytoplasmic foci in C. elegans embryos that resembled P bodies (Richard Davis, personal communication). DCAP-2 is the mammalian and yeast homolog of subunit Dcp2 of decapping enzymes that localizes at P bodies. Staining using this antibody and an anti-GFP antibody indicated that AIN-1 was colocalized with DCAP-2 in the embryos. AIN-1::GFP was also observed to be colocalized with a FLAG-tagged DCAP-1 protein at cytoplasmic foci in C. elegans larvae. DCAP-1 is a homolog of mammalian and yeast Dcp1 that are also a subunit of decapping enzymes localized at P bodies."
Transgene	"WBTransgene00028788"

Expr_pattern : "Expr3649"
Antibody
Antibody_info	"WBAntibody00000509"
GO_term	"GO:0045202"
Gene	"WBGene00004215"
Reference	"WBPaper00026711"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00004215"
Subcellular_localization	"PTP-3 was concentrated at the nerve ring and along the nerve cords in larval and adult animals and showed a punctate pattern. Along the nerve cord, PTP-3 was adjacent to but did not overlap UNC-49. Within the neurons, PTP-3 partially overlapped the SNT-1-containing domain but was concentrated at the edges of the SNT-1 staining. There was a precise colocalization of PTP-3 with SYD-2 and UNC-10. More specifically, a smaller punctum of PTP-3 was observed in or near the center of each of the larger SYD-2 puncta. These data indicate that PTP-3 is predominantly associated with the presynaptic density. To address whether PTP-3 localization was dependent on synaptic vesicles, the accumulation of SNT-1, PTP-3, and UNC-10 were analyzed in unc-104(e1265) kinesin mutants, which causes synaptic vesicles to be retained in cell bodies. PTP-3 and UNC-10 puncta showed colocalization in regions of the nerve cord lacking synaptic vesicles. Thus, like other presynaptic density components, PTP-3 appears to be trafficked to synapses independent of synaptic vesicles."

Expr_pattern : "Expr3650"
GO_term	"GO:0045202"
Gene	"WBGene00004215"
Reference	"WBPaper00026711"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00004215"
Reporter_gene
Subcellular_localization	"PTP-3B::GFP showed a temporally regulated expression, with high expression throughout embryogenesis and larval development until the L1-L2 larval transition. In the adult nervous system, PTP-3B::GFP was present in the nerve ring and along axons of the ventral and dorsal nerve cords and was also observed in the pharyngeal epithelium and the developing uterus throughout development. Most of the PTP-3B::GFP was adjacent to the UNC-10 puncta, with only a small amount of GFP overlapping with UNC-10. PTP-3A::GFP expression was first detected around the 2-fold stage of embryonic development (450 min after fertilization) in the nerve ring and nerve cords and continued at a constant level through larval development. PTP-3A::GFP was seen in a punctate pattern along nerve processes and overlapped with UNC-10 in a pattern that was similar to the endogenous protein. These results suggest that PTP-3A is the major isoform that is localized to presynaptic domains. Consistent with this conclusion, in ptp-3A(ok244) mutant animals, <25% of the UNC-10 puncta (n = 200) contained any PTP-3, and the amount of PTP-3 present at those UNC-10 puncta was reduced."
Transgene	"WBTransgene00028789"

