Pattern	"Compared to wild-type expression, ccf-1 is present at a higher level (148%) in fem-1(lf) adults that produce oocytes but no sperm. ccf-1 expression is reduced in fem-3(gf) (52%) and glp-4(lf) (31%) which produce sperm but no oocytes and have a severely reduced and undifferentiated germline, respectively. The higher expression of ccf-1 in fem-3(gf) than in glp-4 adults could suggest a weak expression of ccf-1 in the male germline. Altogether these results suggest that ccf-1, although present at all stages, is expressed at a higher level in embryos and adults, in which expression is dependant upon the germ line."
Reference	"WBPaper00026675"
