Expr_pattern : "Expr3715"
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0005270" Certain
Gene	"WBGene00001456"
Pattern	"Transgenic animals carrying a gfp reporter gene fused to the promoter region of flp-13 (Pflp-13::gfp) (strain NY1121) show GFP expression in six cell bodies in the ventral nerve cord. Their positions correspond to that of the six DD motor neurons. To confirm their identities, Pflp-13::gfp animals were simultaneously stained with antisera against GABA (red) and GFP (green). Within the ventral nerve cord, six neurons were consistently observed that colocalized GABA and the Pflp-13::GFP (yellow). These are the cell bodies of the six DD motor neurons. Thirteen additional motor neurons were stained by the GABA antibody (red) but not by the antibody to GFP in Pflp-13::gfp animals. These correspond in position and number to the VD mns. Thus, flp-13::gfp reporter represents a gene that is expressed in the DD but not in the VD motor neurons."
Reference	"WBPaper00025150"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00001456"
Reporter_gene
Transgene	"WBTransgene00028841"

Expr_pattern : "Expr3716"
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0005813" Certain
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0006761" Certain
Gene	"WBGene00006843"
Pattern	"[myo-3::unc-119(cDNA)-gfp]: Direct observation of GFP fluorescence resulting from these constructs showed that the cDNA construct was strongly expressed exclusively in body wall and head muscles. No neural expression was detected and coelomocytes could not be seen behind the very bright muscle expression."
Pattern	"myo-3::unc-119(genomicDNA)-gfp: The unc-119 gDNA constructs in combination with the myo-3 promoter resulted in expression in only a few unidentified neurons at a very low level that was insufficient to rescue movement and dauer defects."
Reference	"WBPaper00025188"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00006843"
Remark	"This led to two separate conclusions. First, expressing the UNC-119 protein only in body wall and head muscles is sufficient to partially rescue gross phenotypic defects such as movement and dauer formation. Second, the precise expression of UNC-119 is controlled by a combination of promoter and enhancer elements in a manner that is not strictly additive, but is a synthesis of signals from various regulatory elements."
Reporter_gene
Transgene	"WBTransgene00028842"

