Expr_pattern : "Expr3743"
Antibody
Antibody_info	"WBAntibody00000952"
GO_term	"GO:0043186"
Gene	"WBGene00000479"
Reference	"WBPaper00026857"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00000479"
Subcellular_localization	"Throughout the gonad CGH-1 associates with P granules, as revealed by its overlapping localization with the constitutive P granule component PGL-1. CGH-1 staining levels increase dramatically in response to meiosis entry, and CGH-1 particles that are independent of P granules then accumulate within the core."

Expr_pattern : "Expr3744"
Antibody
Antibody_info	"WBAntibody00000951"
GO_term	"GO:0005737"
GO_term	"GO:0043186"
GO_term	"GO:0044444"
Gene	"WBGene00012484"
Reference	"WBPaper00026857"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00012484"
Subcellular_localization	"CAR-1 levels were modest in the proliferating stem cells at the distal end of the gonad, then increased upon entry into meiosis. Throughout the gonad some CAR-1 staining was localized to perinuclear particles, where it overlapped substantially with staining for CGH-1 and PGL-1. After germ cells entered meiosis, CAR-1 appeared in cytoplasmic granules within the syncytial gonad core, in parallel with CGH-1. Within the core, most CAR-1 particles colocalized with CGH-1, although some distinct CAR-1 and CGH-1 foci were also present."

