Remark	"No signal was detected in cogc-3(k181) mutants, indicating that anti-COGC-3 specifically detected COGC-3 in situ."
Subcellular_localization	"COGC-3 staining was often prominent in the perinuclear region, which may correspond to the ER or Golgi apparatus. The intracellular distribution of COGC-3 was examined in the body wall muscle cells using a Golgi enzyme, MIG-23\/NDPase (a type II membrane protein), as a marker. Some of the anti-COGC-3 signal colocalized with MIG-23-GFP, in particular, at the perinuclear region. The colocalization of the COGC-3 and YFP-TRAM, an ER-marker in the body wall muscle cells, was analyzed. COGC-3 was widely distributed in the cytoplasm and partially colocalized with YFP-TRAM."

