Pattern	"Nine independent transgenic lines carrying the lsy-2::gfp extrachromosomal array displayed gfp expression in all cells and tissue types of the worm, including ASEL and ASER. Expression is first observed at the 50-cell stage, and persists throughout embryogenesis, larval stages and adulthood. This expression pattern relates to endogenous gene function, as lsy-2::gfp transgenes can rescue the sterility and lsy phenotype of lsy-2 null mutants. A similar ubiquitous expression pattern is observed in animals expressing gfp under the control of only the 5' upstream region of the lsy-2 locus."
Reference	"WBPaper00027031"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00003087"
Reporter_gene
Subcellular_localization	"Notably, LSY-2::GFP was localized to moving punctae in the nuclei, which is consistent with a role for lsy-2 in regulating gene expression."
