Remark	"Authors also generated a transgene, Pglr-1::kel-8::yfp, that expresses (via the glr-1 promoter) KEL-8 protein fused at its carboxy terminus to YFP. Pglr-1::kel-8::yfp was introduced as an extra-chromosomal transgene into kel-8 mutant nematodes that express an integrated glr-1::cfp transgene. Although kel-8 mutants accumulate large accretions of GLR-1::CFP in the absence of exogenous KEL-8 protein, sibling kel-8 mutants that express KEL-8::YFP from a Pglr-1::kel-8::yfp transgene have properly-localized GLR-1::CFP (4 independent lines, 15 - 20 animals examined per line). These results indicate that the KEL-8 fusion protein is functional."
Reporter_gene
Subcellular_localization	"KEL-8::GFP was localized to clusters along the ventral cord neurites. Coexpression of KEL-8::GFP and GLR-1::RFP resulted in KEL-8::GFP clusters that were localized adjacent to GLR-1::RFP clusters."
Transgene	"WBTransgene00028893"

