Pattern	"daf-36::gfp was most strikingly expressed in the intestinal cytoplasm at all postembryonic stages, including dauer. In addition, daf-36::gfp was seen in the head mesodermal cell. Occasionally, very faint expression was seen within two unidentified head neurons, posterior to the nerve ring, which were clearly distinct from the XXXR\/L. During the L2d stage, prior to entry into dauer diapause, neuronal expression increased slightly, and, surprisingly, expression commenced in the seam cells, epidermal cells located at the lateral midline."
