Life_stage	"WBls:0000038"
Life_stage	"WBls:0000041"
Pattern	"SIR-2.1::GFP is primarily localized in the nucleus and expression is in most if not all neurons in the head and tail from embryo to adult. SIR-2.1::GFP is seen in many pharyngeal cells, where there is no expression of DAF-16::GFP. SIR-2.1::GFP is also expressed in the hypodermis and first seen at the three-fold stage of embryogenesis, diminished by late L3, and low or off in young adults. SIR-2.1::GFP expression was not observed in the intestine and germ line."
Reference	"WBPaper00026947"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00004800"
Remark	"Several integrated transgenic lines were examined under a fluorescent microscope and showed similar patterns of expression. This SIR-2.1::GFP is functional as it rescues the unc-13(s69); sir-2.1(ok434) strain for life span."
Reporter_gene
Subcellular_localization	"SIR-2.1::GFP is primarily localized in the nucleus."
Transgene	"WBTransgene00004932"

