Gene	"WBGene00003142"
Pattern	"Expressed in throughout embryogenesis. In adult hermaphrodites, MAU-8\/PhLP expression was detected in most tissues, including body wall muscles, hypodermal cells, pharynx and intestine. MAU-8\/PhLP also remained associated with the germline lineage throughout the life of the worm. Staining appears throughout the gonad as small punctate structures concentrated in the cytoplasm and the cortex of oocytes and germline cells."
Reference	"WBPaper00027195"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00003142"
Subcellular_localization	"During embryonic development, from the first cell stage to the end of morphogenesis, MAU-8\/PhLP staining was faint and diffuse in the cytoplasm and strongly concentrated at the cell membranes. In addition, MAU-8\/PhLP exhibits a dynamic cell-cycle-dependent distribution with staining concentrated at the centrosomes and at the central spindle region of mitotic cells. From the 2-cell stage, MAU-8\/PhLP is specifically expressed in the germline blastomere where it co-immunolocalized with P granules."

