Pattern	"This expression pattern, which is confined to late larval stages and adults, has several components. The most obvious and common component is strong non-nuclear expression in the pharynx. Other less common components consist of expression in the head and tail ganglia and ventral-nerve cord, expression in body-wall muscle, and expression in the hypodermis. This gene has homology to tRNA synthases."
