Subcellular_localization	"Whole-mount staining with SYD-9 antibodies showed specific staining in the nuclei of neurons and muscles in WT animals, whereas in ju49 and ok1110 animals, the staining either disappeared completely or was drastically reduced. Both antibodies revealed staining patterns enriched at specific subdomains within the nuclei. The C-terminal antibody detected a speckle-like pattern exclusively in the nuclei. The N-terminal antibody stained a broader region but also included the speckle-like pattern in the nuclei, suggesting that SYD-9 isoforms may have slightly different subcellular distribution."

