Remark	"More detailed studies are required to identify the cellular domains in which STIM-1::GFP is expressed. It should be noted here that the absence of detectable STIM-1::GFP expression in tissues other than those shown does not rule out a functional role for STIM-1 in other cell types. The 1.9-kb stim-1 promoter used in these studies may lack regulatory information required for cell-specific expression. In addition, STIM-1::GFP expression levels may be below detection levels in other tissues. More definitive identification of STIM-1 expression sites awaits the development of suitable antibodies for immunolocalization."
Reporter_gene
Subcellular_localization	"Intestinal STIM-1::GFP appeared to be localized to membrane and submembrane regions. Confocal Z-sections also revealed a prominent punctate localization in the anterior intestine and sheath cells. STIM-1::GFP expression showed a striking localization to a reticular structure in the posterior intestine. This reticular structure resembles the ER of C. elegans intestinal cells."
Transgene	"WBTransgene00012227"

