Pattern	"In gonads of either L4 or young adult wild-type hermaphrodites, CPB-3 was barely detectable at the most distal end, was gradually expressed in the mitotic region, and reached high levels in the transition zone and the pachytene region. Its expression was then gradually decreased in the proximal pachytene region, and no staining was observed in mature sperm and oocytes."
Reference	"WBPaper00027619"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00000772"
Remark	"No detailed description on cellular expression pattern in other tissues."
Subcellular_localization	"Staining of dissected gonads with anti-CPB-3 antibodies appeared specific because no substantial signal was detected in the cpb-3(tm1746) mutant. CPB-3 was stained predominantly in the cytoplasm."

