Subcellular_localization	"Localized to chromosome-associated foci that were most prominent in the transition zone and very early pachytene. Often localized to three to four foci at the onset of meiosis and, by early pachytene, were usually observed at two foci. Colocalization with HIM-8 staining indicate that the foci of ZIM protein corresponded to autosomal pairing centers, most probably to the chromosomes that missegregate in the corresponding mutants."

