Pattern	"Using a full-length pha-4 complementary DNA translation fusion to GFP under the pha-4 promoter, nuclear localization of PHA-4 was observed during development and adulthood in the developing pharynx and in the intestines and also found in the adult worm in a few neuronal cells in the head and tail, which were not found in the developing animal. This expression pattern did not change in response to dietary restriction, and PHA-4 seemed constitutively nuclear under all conditions tested."
