Pattern	"glo-1::gfp expression was first detected in the daughters of the E blastomere (the E2 stage) that produces the entire intestine. Expression continued in all cells of the embryonic and adult intestines. Expression of GLO-1::GFP was never observed in embryonic or adult stage hypodermal (skin) cells. Thus GLO-1 is localized in structures that are consistent with lysosomes and that GLO-1::GFP is an accurate reporter for GLO-1 localization in intestinal cells."
