Expr_pattern : "Expr4952"
GO_term	"GO:0030424"
GO_term	"GO:0045202"
Gene	"WBGene00017195"
Reference	"WBPaper00030940"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00017195"
Remark	"Picture: Figure 2."
Reporter_gene
Subcellular_localization	"Coimmunostaining showed that in the ventral nerve cord, GLO-4::GFP was localized to discrete puncta adjacent to the SV protein SNT-1. In the cholinergic SAB motor neurons, GLO-4::GFP was localized at the anterior tip of the axon, while SNT-1 was localized at puncta throughout the length of the axon and excluded from the tip. This localization pattern is very similar to that of RPM-1. Coimmunostained GLO-4::GFP and endogenous RPM-1 and showed significant colocalization in the ventral cord, especially in regions that had high expression of RPM-1 Similarly, in the SAB neurons, GLO-4::GFP and RPM-1 colocalized at the anterior tip of the axon, where RPM-1 is most concentrated. To further confirm the colocalization of these two proteins at individual synapses in another type of neuron, authors expressed RPM-1::GFP and Cherry::GLO-4 in the type D GABAergic motor neurons using the unc-25 promoter. The D neurons form en passant synapses along the dorsal and ventral nerve cords. Cherry::GLO-4 and RPM-1::GFP colocalized to distinct puncta in the axons of these neurons."
Transgene	"WBTransgene00029573"

