Life_stage	"WBls:0000038"
Life_stage	"WBls:0000041"
Pattern	"Staining behind terminal bulb of pharynx in adults, believed to be the lobes of the excretory gland cell. L1 larvae appear to have nuclear localised staining of the intestine cells."
Pattern	"There are multiple components to the b-galactosidase expression pattern driven by pUL#161G10. The most striking component is in the excretory gland cell, from late embryogenesis onwards. b-galactosidase appears to fill the two large lobes of this bi-nucleated cell which is formed from the fusion of two cells during development. Occasionally the b-galactosidase appears to be in discrete subcellular compartments restricted to the posterior half of the lobes of the excretory gland. There is also expression in the ventral nerve cord from late embryogenesis onwards and in the intestine in the late embryo and early larval stages."
Person	"WBPerson266"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00003986"
Remark	"Reporter fusion junction is at position 24742 in K05B2 ..CATAGAGAGATTTCAGAATCGGACGGACTGCCGTTTCATCGGTCACTTATTATGAACTTACTTACTGTGG CCCACTAGTCAGTGCACTTGCAACAATATGAACAGCGTTATGTAGTTATGCGGGAGGATTGATCTCTGGAAT AGCATTTATGATTGCACCAGCATCTCCAAATATTTATGTATTTATGTTGATTTACGGAGTGATGGGAGGTCT TGGATTTGGTATGATC\/lacZ"
Remark	"fusion junction is at position 24742 in K05B2..CATAGAGAGATTTCAGAATCGGACGGACTGCCGTTTCATCGGTCACTTATTATGAACTTACTTACTGTGGCCCACTAGTCAGTGCACTTGCAACAATATGAACAGCGTTATGTAGTTATGCGGGAGGATTGATCTCTGGAATAGCATTTATGATTGCACCAGCATCTCCAATATTTATGTATTTATGTTGATTTACGGAGTGATGGGAGGTCTTGGATTTGGTATGATC\/lacZ. Other authors: \"Arnold JM\", \"Herbert R\" \"Hope IA\"Date	 1993-01"
Remark	"updated information 01\/98"
