GO_term	"GO:0005886"
Gene	"WBGene00000168"
Life_stage	"WBls:0000005"
Pattern	"APX-1 protein is detected first in the late 2-cell stage at the anterior periphery of P1. It is found in and EMS at the 4-cell stage. Later, it is seen faintly in P3."
Reference	"WBPaper00002479"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00000168"
Remark	"early embryo(author) = blastula embryo(curator)."
Strain	"WBStrain00000001"
Subcellular_localization	"APX-1 was mainly plasma membrane-associated, but punctate patterns below the membrane and in the cytoplasm. APX-1 is seen in the membrane where P1 contacts AB.p, and the punctate structures are present where P1 contacts AB.a and AB.p. In early 4-cell stage embryos, APX-1 staining is seen where P2 contacts AB.p and in punctate structures in P2 and in the cytoplasm of EMS.APX-1 is not detected in AB.a or AB.p. At the 12-cell stage, APX-1 is detected faintly in P3 cytoplasm only. Later, APX-1 appears in a few unidentified cells."

