Antibody	"anti-PIE-1 mouse monoclonal antibodies"
Antibody
Antibody_info	"WBAntibody00000189"
GO_term	"GO:0005634"
GO_term	"GO:0005737"
GO_term	"GO:0005813"
GO_term	"GO:0043186"
Gene	"WBGene00004027"
In_Situ
In_situ	"Digoxigenin labeled DNA probes"
Life_stage	"WBls:0000005"
Life_stage	"WBls:0000041"
Pattern	"In oocytes,1-cell and 2-cell stage embryos, pie-1 mRNA is distributed uniformly. After the 4-cell stage, pie-1 mRNA was lost from somatic blastomeres and remained in the germ lineage. PIE-1 protein was first detected in maturing oocytes, where it is uniformly distributed. PIE-1 level increase during the one cell stage. PIE-1 protein also exists in P1, P2 P3, P4, Z2 and Z3. In P4, PIE-1 is found equally in the P4 daughters (Z2 and Z3) in contrast to earlier divisions in which PIE-1 is localized to the posterior cytoplasm and posterior centrosomes during mitosis."
Reference	"WBPaper00003175"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00004027"
Remark	"early embryo(author) = blastula embryo(curator)."
Strain	"WBStrain00000001"
Subcellular_localization	"A subset of PIE-1 molecules are associated with P granules, but there is a diffuse cytoplasmic component of PIE-1 staining in contrast to the punctate P granule pattern. PIE-1 protein is cytoplasmic until the 2-cell stage, after which it is increasingly nuclear. PIE-1 protein distribution in P0, P1, P2 and P3 follows a similar pattern: initially uniform cytoplasmic distribution, followed by asymmetric cytoplasmic localization at the time of P granule migration, and asymmetric cytoplasmic and centralsomal localizations during mitosis."

