Pattern	"At the 200-cell stage, four posterior ventral cells stain, AB.p(r\/)lpppp(a\/p). At about 350 cells, their eight descendants, and about 12 other cells including lateral and ventral epidermal blast cells, show expression. By the 1.5-fold stage, additional cells stain, e.g., posterior ventral cord neuronal precursors. Most of the cells continue to stain at L1, with the notable exception of the eight descendants of the four cells that show initial staining."
