Expr_pattern : "Expr628"
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0005733"
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0005772" Certain
Gene	"WBGene00000996"
In_Situ
In_situ	"Digoxigenin labeled DNA probe."
Life_stage	"WBls:0000003"
Pattern	"1-28 cell embryo, staining present in all cells (probably represents maternal dif-1 RNA). 58 cell stage, staining ceases in all but the gut progenitor cells, gut expression continues throughout embryogenesis. At this stage gut staining becomes stronger. ~200 cell stage, dif-1 RNA detected in hypodermal cells and persists until hypodermal cells begin to enclose the embryo (it is not clear if hypodermal expression persists after this time). Expression in hypodermis starts after the decay of dif-1 RNA in all but gut precursor cells. 550 cell stage, detected only in gut and hypodermal cells early morphogenesis, strong expression in gut but weak in hypodermis."
Reference	"WBPaper00002188"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00000996"
Remark	"See Expr629 for Expr_pattern for the same locus."
Remark	"This information was extracted from published material (Archana Sharma-Oates, Andrew Mounsey and Ian A. Hope)."

