Antibody	"Anti-pal-1 antibodies were purified from the sera of two rabbits immunized with a PAL-1:(his) fusion protein by blot affinity purification."
Antibody
Antibody_info	"WBAntibody00000128"
Gene	"WBGene00003912"
Life_stage	"WBls:0000005"
Life_stage	"WBls:0000008"
Life_stage	"WBls:0000010"
Pattern	"High levels in P2 and EMS (posterior nuclei) at the 4-cell stage. From 4-cell to the 24-cell stage, PAL-1 is detected in all descendants of both P2 and EMS. The PAL-1 antibody stained the nuclei throughout the cell cycle and was localized to the condensed chromosomes during mitosis. At the 24-cell stage, the level of staining intensity increased in the two C descendants, Ca and Cp. In 28-cell embryos strong staining was observed in the four C descendants and lower levels of staining was also observed in D and P4. At the 28-cell stage expression was stronger in P2 than in EMS descendants."
Reference	"WBPaper00002573"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00003912"
Remark	"See Expr746 for in situ data."
Remark	"This information was extracted from published material (Archana Sharma-Oates, Andrew Mounsey and Ian A. Hope)."

