Antibody_info	"WBAntibody00001263"
Antibody_info	"WBAntibody00001264"
GO_term	"GO:0000793"
Gene	"WBGene00006377"
Reference	"WBPaper00030764"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00006377"
Remark	"Picture: Figure 2."
Subcellular_localization	"SYP-3 is observed colocalizing with SYP-1 at bright foci present in the first few nuclei upon entrance into meiosis. This initial colocalization at bright foci is followed by an extensive localization of SYP-3 along chromosomes during early to mid-transition zone, while chromosomes are still in the clustered organization characteristic of this stage. This is distinct from the localization pattern observed for either SYP-1 or SYP-2, which are restricted to short or discontinuous stretches along chromosomes until halfway between mid- and late transition zone. However, short stretches of SYP-1 immunostaining were observed only along regions exhibiting extensive SYP-3 association. Upon entrance into pachytene, SYP-3 localizes continuously at the interface between paired and aligned homologous chromosomes, similarly to SYP-1 and SYP-2. As nuclei progress through late prophase and the SC disassembles, SYP-3 localization is the same as that observed for SYP-1 and SYP-2. SYP-3 chromosomal association is progressively reduced, becoming restricted to the mid-bivalents in early diakinesis, and is no longer apparent at the last oocyte prior to fertilization."

