Pattern	"In wild-type hermaphrodites 24 hr post mid-L4, total MPK-1 is found throughout the germline, with slightly lower levels in the distal-most end and slightly higher levels in the proximal region. dpMPK-1(diphosphorylated activated) is undetectable in the mitotic and transition zone regions, peaks in the proximal part of pachytene, becomes low but detectable in the loop region, and peaks again in diakinesis oocytes in the proximal gonad."
Reference	"WBPaper00031318"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00003401"
Remark	"Picture: Figure 1A, 2A."
Subcellular_localization	"Total MPK-1 is primarily cytoplasmic except in late-stage oocytes where there is nuclear enrichment."

Expr_pattern : "Expr7891"
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0003681" Certain
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0003721" Certain
