Life_stage	"WBls:0000038"
Life_stage	"WBls:0000041"
Pattern	"GFP signal was detected in pharyngeal, intestinal, and hypodermal cells that are known to function as phagocytes during embryogenesis. Robust GFP expression was observed in most if not all neurons, including head, ventral cord, and tail neurons in larvae and adults coexpressing Punc-108 gfp::unc-108(+) and a neural-specific Prab-3 rfp reporter."
Reference	"WBPaper00031470"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00006833"
Remark	"Picture: Fig. 3."
Reporter_gene
Transgene	"WBTransgene00030225"

Expr_pattern : "Expr7948"
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0003984" Certain
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0003985" Certain
Gene	"WBGene00013974"
Life_stage	"WBls:0000024"
Life_stage	"WBls:0000027"
Life_stage	"WBls:0000035"
Life_stage	"WBls:0000038"
Life_stage	"WBls:0000057"
Pattern	"GFP fluorescence was observed in paired neurons situated in the head region around the posterior pharyngeal bulb. The unique morphology suggested that expression was in the AIB interneuron pair. Based on cell position, DiI staining, costaining, and morphology authors concluded that npr-9 is expressed in the AIB interneuron. No GFP fluorescence was noted in somatic gonad tissue, vulval muscle, body wall, and inner labial neurons. An identical pattern of head neuron GFP expression was noted during all larval stages (L1, L2, L3, and L4) and in hermaphrodite adults. There was no GFP expression detected in embryos."
Reference	"WBPaper00031455"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00013974"
Remark	"Picture: Figure 1 A, B."
Reporter_gene
Transgene	"WBTransgene00030226"

Expr_pattern : "Expr7949"
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0003681" Partial
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0005300" Uncertain
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0005319" Certain
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0005739" Partial
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0005753" Certain
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0006748" Certain
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0006759" Partial
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0006760" Certain
Gene	"WBGene00000149"
Life_stage	"WBls:0000038"
Life_stage	"WBls:0000041"
Pattern	"GFP signals were observed in the head and pharynx, spermatheca, uterus and vulva, some cells in tail and ventral neurons. Strong GFP expression was observed in seam cells. Furthermore, apl-1 expression in seam cells was temporally regulated. The GFP signal in seam cells was not detected (or in rare cases, weakly detected) from L1 to early L4 stages, frequently detected from the mid L4 stage, and almost always detected with high-level expression at late L4 and adult stages. This temporal expression profile of apl-1 was observed in two independent integrated lines of apl-1::gfp::unc-54. No temporal change of apl-1 expression was apparent in any other cells)."
Reference	"WBPaper00031506"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00000149"
Remark	"Picture: Figure 3, S3, S4."
Reporter_gene
Transgene	"WBTransgene00005001"
Transgene	"WBTransgene00005002"

Expr_pattern : "Expr7950"
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0005300" Certain
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0005733" Certain
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0005751" Certain
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0005772" Certain
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0005828" Certain
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0006751" Certain
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0006759" Certain
GO_term	"GO:0005764"
GO_term	"GO:0005768"
Gene	"WBGene00006833"
Life_stage	"WBls:0000004"
Life_stage	"WBls:0000010"
Life_stage	"WBls:0000013"
Life_stage	"WBls:0000015"
Life_stage	"WBls:0000021"
Life_stage	"WBls:0000024"
Life_stage	"WBls:0000027"
Life_stage	"WBls:0000035"
Life_stage	"WBls:0000038"
Life_stage	"WBls:0000041"
Pattern	"unc-108::gfp was ubiquitously expressed in the embryo, starting from the very early stage of 50 to 100 cells and throughout the larval and adult stages. The expression of unc-108::gfp was observed in engulfing cells, such as hypodermal cells, intestine cells and gonadal sheath cells. unc-108::gfp was also seen in many head and tail neurons as well as ventral cord neurons. unc-108 is also expressed in the coelomocytes. Similar expression patterns with more-vesicular localizations were observed in animals expressing GFP::UNC-108 fusion protein."
Reference	"WBPaper00031498"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00006833"
Remark	"Picture: Figure 3 and S3."
Reporter_gene
Subcellular_localization	"GFP::UNC-108 was observed on endosomes where it overlapped with mCHERRY::RAB-5 and on lysosomes marked by mCHERRY::CUP-5."
Transgene	"WBTransgene00030227"

Expr_pattern : "Expr7951"
GO_term	"GO:0030425"
GO_term	"GO:0045202"
Gene	"WBGene00006412"
Reference	"WBPaper00031496"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00006412"
Remark	"Picture: Figure 2."
Reporter_gene
Subcellular_localization	"Bright punctate staining was observed in dendritic (postsynaptic) regions. Clear punctate staining was also observed in presynaptic regions of each neuronal type. For example, in the DA9 motor neuron, bright NLG-1::YFP puncta were present in the ventral postsynaptic domain, and dimmer puncta were present in the dorsal presynaptic region. Puncta were excluded from the synapse-poor region between the cell body and dorsal presynaptic region and from the anterior asynaptic region of the dorsal process. To further study the punctate staining in the presynaptic region, NLG-1::YFP localization was examined in animals expressing the tagged synaptic vesicle protein mCherry::RAB-3 in DA9. In the dorsal axon, NLG-1::YFP puncta partially colocalized with puncta containing mCherry::RAB-3, suggesting that NLG-1::YFP localization is perisynaptic."
Transgene	"WBTransgene00030228"

