Pattern	"Expression was observed in neurons, the pharynx, and the uterine-vulval region. NSF-1S::GFP is highly expressed in neurons, especially in the vicinity of the pharynx, but has no significant expression in the pharynx itself or in the uterine-vulval region. NSF-1L::GFP is mainly expressed in the pharynx and the uterine-vulval region, and is also expressed in the nerve ring but has no significant expression in other neurons."
Reference	"WBPaper00027676"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00003818"
Remark	"Picture: Figs. 5B, C."
Reporter_gene
Transgene	"WBTransgene00030249"

