Subcellular_localization	"In the distal germline, VAB-1::GFP localizes to the plasma membrane of the syncytial germ cells as visualized with an mCherry::PH domain fusion. In proximal oocytes, VAB-1::GFP is predominantly associated with intracellular vesicles both in the interior and at the cortex. The VAB-1::GFP-containing intracellular vesicles vary in size from small puncta to large (0.5 to 1.0 um diameter) ring-like structures. Cortically localized VAB-1::GFP-containing vesicles abut, or are adjacent to, the plasma membrane, and only a small fraction of the VAB-1::GFP signal exhibits colocalization with the mCherry::PH domain plasma-membrane marker."
