Gene	"WBGene00020838"
Pattern	"Several T27A3.1pro::DsRed2-positive cells in the head region of the worms were also pan-neural::gfp-positive, demonstrating that T27A3.1 is indeed expressed in a subset of neurons. T27A3.1pro::DsRed2-positive neurons were first visible late in embryogenesis. Although there were some variations between worms within and between lines, up to seven neurons on each side of the head of the worm expressed T27A3.1. Authors were able to identify another pair of T27A3.1-expressing neurons along the body of the worm as CAN L and R."
Reference	"WBPaper00031987"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00020838"
Remark	"Picture: Figure 4."
