Remark	"The myoepithelial-sheath cells are smooth-muscle-like cells that surround oocytes at the proximal gonad."
Subcellular_localization	"Immunofluorescent signals of UNC-60A was detected in the myoepithelial-sheath cells, which are also positive for MyoA myosin heavy chain, although the UNC-60A signals were much weaker than those in the oocytes (note that signals in the oocytes are saturated). Occasionally, authors found areas in which anti-UNC-60A antibody penetrated only into the myoepithelial sheath but not into the oocytes and were able to observe punctate localization of UNC-60A. These puncta localized along with filamentous actin."

Expr_pattern : "Expr8234"
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0004510" Certain
