Subcellular_localization	"CSNK-1 is associated with the plasma membrane at all stages of the cell cycle. In addition, punctate staining is visible around the asters during mitosis. This staining pattern corresponds to CSNK-1, as it is lost in csnk-1(RNAi) embryos."

Expr_pattern : "Expr8264"
GO_term	"GO:0005737"
GO_term	"GO:0005886"
GO_term	"GO:0005938"
Gene	"WBGene00013709"
Reference	"WBPaper00032096"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00013709"
Remark	"Picture: Figure 3E, Movie S1."
Reporter_gene
Subcellular_localization	"GFP::CSNK-1 localizes at the membrane at all stages. In addition, puncta form at the plasma membrane and move toward the asters. Before polarization, GFP::CSNK-1 appears as small foci and short filaments throughout the cortex. Shortly after polarization, the GFP::CSNK-1 foci move away from the posterior cortex toward the anterior, resulting in an anterior cortical enrichment of the GFP::CSNK-1 foci. Anterior enrichment appears to be sensitive to fixation, as it is not seen for CSNK-1 or GFP::CSNK-1 in fixed samples. To summarize, CSNK-1 is found at the cortex and in cytoplasmic puncta, and a functional GFP tagged protein is anteriorly enriched."
Transgene	"WBTransgene00005050"

Expr_pattern : "Expr8265"
