Expr_pattern : "Expr8387"
Antibody
Antibody_info	"WBAntibody00001483"
GO_term	"GO:0005634"
Gene	"WBGene00013095"
Reference	"WBPaper00032356"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00013095"
Remark	"Picture: Figure 3B, 3C."
Subcellular_localization	"ING-3 was present in the newly-fertilized embryo, where it co-localized with DNA. Similar localization of ING-3 and DAPI continued throughout the cell cycle, including during mitosis in developing embryos. ING-3 was also present in the gonad. Staining was weak in the mitotic proliferating germ cells (region I) but was stronger in the transition zone (region II) and the following early pachytene stages (region III). It decreased by late pachytene and diplotene (region IV). Nuclear ING-3 staining overlapped extensively with DNA, although it was sometimes uneven. Nuclear staining was absent when antisera was pre-incubated with the immunizing peptide as well as in the deletion allele ing-3(tm2530), demonstrating antibody specificity. ING-3 was also expressed in somatic cells where it again overlapped with DAPI, and strong staining was seen for some cells in the anterior gut."

