Subcellular_localization	"GFP::PIE-1 becomes enriched in the posterior, on and around punctate structures known as P granules, which are RNA-rich components of the germplasm. Although GFP::PIE-1 also becomes enriched in pronuclei, the nuclear localization of PIE-1 has been shown to have little effect on cytoplasmic enrichment. Posterior fluorescence intensity reached a plateau value approximately three times the initial prefertilization level, whereas anterior fluorescence intensity decreased to approximately half its initial value. Overall fluorescence intensity in the zygote increased slightly during the first cell division, suggesting a low level of expression throughout the first division."
