GO_term	"GO:0043186"
Gene	"WBGene00020091"
Reference	"WBPaper00033205"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00020091"
Remark	"Picture: 3H to 3M."
Subcellular_localization	"Immunostaining revealed that RNP-8L protein is predominantly cytoplasmic, colocalizes with the PGL-1 germ granule marker, and is abundant in the proximal pachytene region and developing oocytes. RNP-8L was detectable in males, but much less abundant than in hermaphrodites. As assessed by immunocytochemistry of male germlines, RNP-8L was limited to the mitotic region, transition zone, and distal pachytene region; it was absent from proximal pachytene cells, spermatocytes, and mature sperm. RNP-8L was similar in both hermaphrodite and male distal germlines, both with respect to its low level and its distribution in cytoplasmic granules. As assessed by western blot, RNP-8L was also low in mutant adult hermaphrodites that made only sperm and no oocytes. Abundant RNP-8L seem to be associated with oogenesis."

