Gene	"WBGene00015466"
Reference	"WBPaper00035062"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00015466"
Remark	"Picture: Fig 4, Fig S2E."
Subcellular_localization	"HYLS-1 localized to punctate structures in amphid and labial\/cephalic neurons. This punctate staining was absent in hyls-1(D) worms and was fully restored. HYLS-1 puncta were closely apposed to the short stretches of NPH-4:YFP, a marker for the ciliary transition zone, indicating that HYLS-1 localizes to a discrete structure at the base of cilia. This result was confirmed using CHE-GFP, an IFT component that localizes to the transition zone and along the ciliary axoneme. Localization to the base of the cilium was also observed in phasmid neurons. Thus, HYLS-1 localizes to a discrete structure at the base of the mature cilium."

Expr_pattern : "Expr8773"
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0005812" Certain
Gene	"WBGene00003625"
Pattern	"The nhr-31 promoter drives strong expression in the excretory cell (EC). In transgenic animals, GFP protein was first observed in the EC cell shortly after EC birth and persisted in the EC for the remainder of worm embryogenesis, larval development, and adulthood. GFP was observed throughout the cytoplasm of the H-shaped excretory cell."
Reference	"WBPaper00035075"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00003625"
Remark	"Picture: Figure 1B."
Reporter_gene
Transgene	"WBTransgene00030702"

