Expr_pattern : "Expr8806"
Antibody
Antibody_info	"WBAntibody00001990"
GO_term	"GO:0005634"
GO_term	"GO:0005694"
Gene	"WBGene00019247"
Reference	"WBPaper00035253"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00019247"
Remark	"Picture: Fig 3."
Subcellular_localization	"SYP-4 signal was detected on meiotic chromosomes in wild type nuclei but not in syp-4(tm2713) mutants. In wild type, SYP-4 was first detected upon entrance into meiosis as foci or short tracks on chromosomes in transition zone nuclei (Figure 3A). SYP-4 remained associated with chromosomes throughout pachytene where it was observed between synapsed chromosomes. During the transition from late pachytene into diplotene, the SC starts to disassemble and chromosome remodeling unfolds around the crossover site. At this transition, SYP-4 signal was greatly reduced throughout most of the length of the chromosomes, becoming mostly concentrated towards one end of each chromosome. By early diakinesis, SYP-4 localization was restricted to the short axes (short arms; the region distal to the chiasma, and by the end of diakinesis it was no longer detectable on chromosomes."

