Expr_pattern : "Expr8836"
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0005813" Certain
GO_term	"GO:0031430"
Gene	"WBGene00006814"
Pattern	"At the 1.5-fold stage, signal is concentrated in the region of the contractile apparatus, where it overlaps that of myosin. As development continues, the stain becomes organized into longitudinal lines of dots that roughly coincide with the striped myosin pattern. Transgene expression is not limited to body-wall muscle. In embryos, anti-GFP produces signal in areas outside the muscle quadrants. UNC-82::GFP is not detected in the regions of pharyngeal muscle cells that are occupied by thick filaments. Instead, signal is located between the bands of anti-UNC-89 stain. This location is consistent with expression of UNC-82 in marginal cells, or with localization in muscle near the cell membrane that contacts either a marginal cell or the cuticle lining the pharyngeal lumen."
Reference	"WBPaper00035423"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00006814"
Remark	"Picture: Figure 5."
Reporter_gene
Subcellular_localization	"UNC-82::GFP colocalizes with UNC-89, indicating that the fusion protein is present at or near the M-line. UNC-82::GFP fluorescence in the M-line region is detected throughout the depth of the myofilament lattice. The distribution of UNC-82::GFP appears punctate by antibody staining in fragmented adults, but as continuous lines when viewed by endogenous GFP fluorescence in living adults or in peroxide-tube-fixed specimens."
Transgene	"WBTransgene00030740"

Expr_pattern : "Expr8837"
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0006797" Certain
Antibody
Antibody_info	"WBAntibody00002049"
GO_term	"GO:0005634"
GO_term	"GO:0005938"
Gene	"WBGene00020035"
Gene	"WBGene00020652"
Reference	"WBPaper00035427"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00020035"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00020652"
Remark	"Picture: Figure 4B, 4C, Figure S6"
Subcellular_localization	"EGG-4\/5 localize to the cortex of oocytes. In addition, EGG-4\/5 were also detected in oocyte nuclei. The cortical and nuclear signals were eliminated by RNAi codepletion of EGG-4 and EGG-5, confirming that they correspond to endogenous EGG-4\/5. Staining of hermaphrodites homozygous for single deletions in either EGG-4 or EGG-5 gave the same pattern as wild-type, confirming that EGG-4 and EGG-5 are both expressed in oocytes. In zygotes in meiosis II, EGG-4\/5 were enriched on subcortical puncta, also positive for EGG-3. EGG-3-positive puncta invade the cytoplasm during meiosis II. EGG-4\/5 puncta, in contrast, were prominent only near the cortex and around the sperm pronucleus. No EGG-4\/5 were detected above background in 2-cell embryos."

Expr_pattern : "Expr8838"
Antibody
Antibody_info	"WBAntibody00002051"
GO_term	"GO:0005938"
Gene	"WBGene00000203"
Life_stage	"WBls:0000005"
Reference	"WBPaper00035433"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00000203"
Remark	"Picture: Fig 2."
Subcellular_localization	"Enrichment of ARX-5 was found near plasma membranes. This pattern was seen at gastrulation and earlier, and it was eliminated using RNAi targeting arx-5. At the time of Ea\/p cell internalization, ARX-5 was also present at sites where MS granddaughter cells contact Ea at the apical surfaces of the cells. Diffuse cytoplasmic and P-granule staining was also seen, but RNAi targeting arx-5 eliminated only the cortical signal, suggesting that the cytoplasmic and P-granule staining were primarily non-specific background. Thus, Arp2\/3 is enriched at the cell cortex at gastrulation and earlier."

