GO_term	"GO:0055037"
Gene	"WBGene00010272"
Reference	"WBPaper00035466"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00010272"
Remark	"Picture: Fig 2, Fig S2, S3."
Subcellular_localization	"Endogenous AMPH-1 colocalizes extensively with endogenous RME-1 on tubulovesicular basolateral recycling endosomes, and on more weakly labelled sub-apical structures of the worm intestine, possibly the apical recycling endosomes. Although there was significant overlap of RME-1 and AMPH-1 labelling on the recycling endosome, the two proteins did not label the endosome identically. Endogenous AMPH-1 also colocalized with basolateral GFP-tagged SDPN-1 (a C. elegans homologue of synaptic dynamin binding protein, also known as pacsin), another marker for the C. elegans recycling endosome. Anti-AMPH-1 staining failed to colocalize with markers for clathrin-coated pits (GFP-tagged CHC-1\/clathrin), early endosomes (GFPRAB-5), late endosomes (GFPRAB-7) or the Golgi (mannosidaseGFP), indicating that AMPH-1 is specifically enriched on recycling endosomes. Extensive colocalization of mCherryRME-1 and AMPH-1GFP was also observed in living transgenic animals, supporting the data derived from fixed tissue."

