Expr_pattern : "Expr9012"
Antibody
Antibody_info	"WBAntibody00002132"
GO_term	"GO:0043186"
Gene	"WBGene00011580"
Reference	"WBPaper00036048"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00011580"
Remark	"Picture: Fig 3A, 3F, 3G, 4A, 4B."
Subcellular_localization	"Anti-DDX-19 showed low levels of staining at the nuclear rim and in the cytoplasm of somatic cells but much stronger staining on germ nuclei; staining diminished or disappeared on late oogonial nuclei that cease transcription. At high magnification, DDX-19 appeared concentrated in patches on both adult and larval germ nuclei."
Subcellular_localization	"Co-staining with anti-NPP-9 and anti-PGL-1 showed that the vast majority of DDX-19 was localized at Pg-NPCs(nuclear pore complexes): in the data set of 100 large patches of NPP-9, 94% of the P granule-positive patches colocalized with a patch of DDX-19. The profile of each DDX-19 patch typically was smaller than the associated patch of NPP-9 but similar to that of PGL-1. In cross-sections of nuclei, DDX-19 appeared concentrated between the zones of PGL-1 and NPP-9, forming a tripartite sandwich; remarkably, P granules initially maintained a similar, tripartite appearance after detaching from oogonia nuclei."

Expr_pattern : "Expr9013"
Antibody
Antibody_info	"WBAntibody00002133"
GO_term	"GO:0005643"
GO_term	"GO:0005730"
Gene	"WBGene00003834"
Reference	"WBPaper00036048"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00003834"
Remark	"Picture: Fig 5."
Subcellular_localization	"Anti-NXF-1 showed strong staining at the nuclear rim of somatic cells and germ cells. Co-staining experiments with anti-PGL-1 and anti-NXF-1 showed that nearly all the NXF-1 at the rim of germ nuclei is present at Pg-NPCs(nuclear pore complexes): surface views of nuclei showed a P granule in close association with the prominent patches of NXF-1 and cross-sections showed that NXF-1 was concentrated at the bases of P granules. In addition to staining at the nuclear rim, anti-NXF-1 stained foci at the center of most germ nuclei, a region occupied by the nucleolus. NXF-1 localization at the nuclear rim was very similar to NPP-9 localization. Indeed, the anti-NXF-1 and anti-NPP-9 antibodies showed strong competition for staining on formaldehyde-fixed nuclei, necessitating the use of a denaturing fixative."

