Reporter_gene
Subcellular_localization	"In the C. elegans intestine, RFP-RAB-10 and GFP-RAB-8 colocalized extensively. Closer examination showed that EHBP-1 colocalized with RAB-10 and RAB-8 on punctate endosomal membranes. EHBP-1 also localized to tubular elements associated with the puncta and the plasma membrane. EHBP-1-GFP also occasionally overlapped with the early endosome marker RFP-RAB-5, but the EHBP-1-GFP labeled structures more often localized near RFP-RAB-5 puncta rather than overlapping with them directly. EHBP-1-GFP was not found to colocalize with the apical recycling marker RFP-RAB-11 or the Golgi marker MANS-RFP. Taken together these results indicate that EHBP-1 is enriched on endosomes."
Subcellular_localization	"The EHBP-1-GFP fusion protein was localized in a punctate or tubular pattern in most tissues. In the intestine, EHBP-1-GFP was localized to both the apical and basolateral plasma membranes. Near basolateral membranes, EHBP-1-GFP labeled distinct cytoplasmic puncta resembling endosomes ranging in size from 0.5 to 1.0 um. In addition to punctate structures, EHBP-1-GFP also labeled tubular structures close to the basolateral plasma membrane of the intestine."
Transgene	"WBTransgene00030890"

