Remark	"Picture: Fig. 1A."
Subcellular_localization	"PAM-1 is a cytoplasmic aminopeptidase present throughout the cell during early development. During meiosis I, PAM-1 localizes to the cytoplasm just under the cell cortex. By meiosis II, this subcortical localization extends to the entire cytoplasm where it is seen throughout early development. During the first cell division and beyond, PAM-1 is enriched around mitotic chromosomes, clearly seen in metaphase and anaphase, and near the spindle poles."

