Remark	"Picture: Fig 2."
Reporter_gene
Subcellular_localization	"Expression in early embryo: GFP::W10G11.20::FLAG was present in the cytoplasm throughout cell cycle. As the cell cycle proceeds, the signal at the nuclear periphery became brighter, and it was also detected around centrosomes. In metaphase, when the nuclear membrane becomes partially permeable, GFP::W10G11.20::FLAG was enriched on both sides of condensed chromosomes (metaphase plates). After cell division, GFP::W10G11.20::FLAG was temporally enriched at the cell boundaries. In addition, GFP::W10G11.20::FLAG localized to the female meiotic spindle."
Subcellular_localization	"Expression in the adult hermaphrodite gonads: While GFP::W10G11.20::FLAG was undetectable in the distal gonad where germ cells are mitotic, it was detected as bright dots at the periphery of nuclei (a few dots per nucleus) in the transition zone. After the pachytene stage, it localized to the entire periphery of the nuclei."
Transgene	"WBTransgene00007849"

