Pattern	"Developing embryos was found carrying ngn-1::gfp and NGN-1::GFP protein was present in the MI mother cell. By contrast, NGN-1::GFP was not detectable in the e3D mother cell, indicating that expression of ngn-1 is left-right asymmetric within this asymmetric cell lineage."
Reference	"WBPaper00037739"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00003595"
Remark	"Picture: Fig. 4A to 4C."
Reporter_gene	"[ngn-1p::ngn-1-gfp] translational fusion. A translational ngn-1::gfp fusion gene was created by an in-frame insertion of a gfp-coding sequence into the 3' end of the ngn-1-coding sequence flanked by the 12.4 kb 5' upstream and 1.5 kb 3 downstream genomic sequence. Authors integrated this ngn-1::gfp transgene into the C. elegans genome and found that the ngn-1::gfp transgene rescued the MI transformation of ngn-1(n1921) mutants (see Table S1A in the supplementary material), indicating that this ngn-1::gfp is functional."
Reporter_gene
Transgene	"WBTransgene00014109"

