Subcellular_localization	"GFP-SNAP-29 and mC-SNAP-29 mainly localized to intracellular punctate structures and the apical and basolateral plasma membranes, but a significant portion of the proteins also seemed to be cytosolic in nature. Most puncta of mC-SNAP-29 extensively colocalized with GFP-SYN-16 and closely attached with GFP-RER-1, suggesting the late-Golgi localization of mC-SNAP-29. Because mC-SNAP-29 was also associated with GFP-RAB-5, mC-SNAP-29 could distribute to the Golgi-associated endosomes. mC-SNAP-29-positive structures were often juxtaposed directly to RME-1-labeled recycling endosomes. These results suggest that a large part of SNAP-29 localizes to the late-Golgi, endosomes, and the plasma membrane."
Transgene	"WBTransgene00031079"

