Pattern	"Expression of this neural pattern is first seen prior to the embryonic comma stage, and extends through to adulthood. Strong staining is seen in the ventral nerve cord and its cell bodies, in the retrovesicular ganglion, the circumpharyngeal nerve ring, and in the rectal muscle group involved in defecation (anal depressor, sphincter muscle and intestinal muscle). The DVB neuron which innervates this muscle group also exhibits staining. Weaker staining can be observed in the dorsal nerve cord and in some commissures possibly of VD or DD type. Staining appears to be in foci along the commissures."
Reference	"WBPaper00005281"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00010096"
Remark	"Legacy Data: \"Bauer PK\" \"Mounsey A\" \"Royall CM\" \"Hope IA\" Date 1997-07."
