Life_stage	"WBls:0000019"
Life_stage	"WBls:0000021"
Life_stage	"WBls:0000022"
Pattern	"In the adult stage, VHA-11 was expressed mainly in an H-shaped excretory cell and also in intestinal cells. Diffuse staining in the cytoplasm could be seen at all embryonic stages. Beginning at the comma stage, dense dot-like staining became clearly visible in intestinal cells and was detectable during embryonic development. These results indicate that V-ATPase is localized in intracellular compartments of embryos, especially those of intestinal cells."
Reference	"WBPaper00004341"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00006920"
Remark	"Adult expression is consistent with expression of the vha-11::GFP reporter gene."
Subcellular_localization	"In embryonic stages, VHA-11 was detected as dot-like intracellular compartments around the nuclei. V-ATPase is localized in intracellular compartments of embryos."

