Life_stage	"WBls:0000021"
Life_stage	"WBls:0000022"
Pattern	"ldb-1b::gfp is expressed throughout the nervous system in larvae and in adults. Moreover it is expressed in developing and adult vulval cells and in adjacent developing and adult uterine cells. In adult male animals, all the neurons of the tail region also express ldb-1b::gfp. Expression analysis of the construct ldb-1a::gfp revealed a temporal and spatial overlapping expression pattern with ldb-1b::gfp. Additional expression is seen in all gonadal sheath cells and adult dorsal body muscle cells and vulval muscles. Embryonic expression of ldb-1 was detected first in 200- to 260-min-old embryos, in which all but the hyp-7 cells express the gfp construct. This ubiquitous expression becomes more restricted to the anterior, ventral, and posterior part in the comma stage embryo, in which all the cells but hyp-7 and the gut express the construct."
Reference	"WBPaper00004360"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00002261"
Remark	"200- to 260-min-old embryos (Author) = late cleavage stage embryo (curator)."
Reporter_gene
Transgene	"WBTransgene00030999"

