Pattern	"Fixed embryos stained with antiCED-9 revealed that CED-9 was present in all cells during C. elegans embryogenesis, beginning as early as the two-cell stage. CED-9 levels peaked at approximately the 200 cell stage and slowly diminished, becoming undetectable around the time of hatching. CED-9 protein was not observed in larvae or adults."
