Life_stage	"WBls:0000041"
Pattern	"LBP-5-GFP was observed in the intestine during all larval stages. The fusion protein was also detected in adult nematodes. Expression in individual seam cells was often highly punctate, and strong GFP expression was observed in these cells in the L4 larval and adult stages. GFP expression was observed during embryogenesis and in all subsequent larval and adult stages. LBP-5 protein was expressed widely in many different cell types, indicating that LBP-5 most likely plays important roles throughout the entire worm body. In particular, LBP-5 expression is high within the hypodermis and intestine, which are major sites of fat accumulation."
Reference	"WBPaper00039781"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00002257"
Reporter_gene
Subcellular_localization	"LBP-5-GFP was detected in large intestinal nuclei, and as punctate staining in the nuclear region of seam cells."
Transgene	"WBTransgene00031094"

