Pattern	"Both anti-VAB-10N and anti-VAB-10B detected signals in wild-type DTCs. Anti-VAB-10A failed to reveal signals even in wild-type DTCs. Although anti-VAB-10N uniformly stained the cytoplasm of DTCs in whole-mount worm preparations, it detected discontinuous filamentous structures in the dissected gonads. These results suggest that the filamentous antigen localization may be susceptible to fixative conditions. Immunohistochemical analysis also revealed that anti-VAB-10A stained fibrous organelles in the epidermis, and anti-VAB-10B detected reciprocal circumferential bands in the epidermis. We also detected signals in the pharynx and body wall muscle using anti-VAB-10B and anti-VAB-10N."
