In_Situ
In_situ	"Single molecule FISH. smFISH was performed as described (Raj et al., 2008). In short, synchronized L1 animals were fixed using 4% formaldehyde and 70% ethanol. Hybridization was done for > 12 h at 30 &deg;C in the dark. Oligonucleotide probes were designed using a specific algorithm (www.singlemoleculefish.com) and chemically coupled to Cy5 (mig-21 probe)."
Pattern	"mig-21 is symmetrically expressed between the two Q neuroblasts. This expression is however transient and restricted to the time period in which the initial polarization and migration of the Q neuroblasts takes place. Thus, within the first two hours after hatching, when the Q neuroblasts have polarized but the cell body has not yet migrated, an average of 25 &plusmn; 4.6 mig-21 transcripts (mean &plusmn; SD, n = 12) were found in QL and 26 &plusmn; 5.0 transcripts in QR (n = 17). At 2-4 h after hatching, when the Q neuroblasts are migrating over their neighboring seam cells, expression decreased slightly, with 17 &plusmn; 5.8 mig-21 transcripts in QL (n = 15) and 21 &plusmn; 6.2 transcripts in QR (n=18). Four to six hours after hatching, when the Q neuroblasts have divided, mig-21 expression was strongly decreased, with 2 &plusmn; 2.4 transcripts in QL (n = 22) and 5 &plusmn; 3.4 transcripts in QR (n=19). In addition to the expression in the Q neuroblasts, mig-21 is also expressed in the four body wall muscle quadrants of L1 stage larvae. In contrast to the expression in the Q neuroblasts, the muscle specific expression of mig-21 persists throughout development."
Reference	"WBPaper00040419"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00003252"

Expr_pattern : "Expr9685"
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0004054" Certain
Anatomy_term	"WBbt:0004056" Certain
Gene	"WBGene00003102"
In_Situ
In_situ	"Single molecule FISH. smFISH was performed as described (Raj et al., 2008). In short, synchronized L1 animals were fixed using 4% formaldehyde and 70% ethanol. Hybridization was done for > 12 h at 30 &deg;C in the dark. Oligonucleotide probes were designed using a specific algorithm (www.singlemoleculefish.com) and chemically coupled to Alexa594 (mab-5 probe)."
Pattern	"Expression of the Wnt target gene mab-5 was examined in Q neuroblasts after initial migration but before Q.d cell migration. Expression of mab-5 was quantified using smFISH in Q neuroblasts and was plotted against the position of the Q neuroblasts on the anteroposterior axis. In wild type animals, mab-5 was expressed at an average of 30 &plusmn; 7.1 (mean &plusmn; SD, n = 32) transcripts per cell in QL, and 3 &plusmn; 2.9 transcripts per cell in QR (n = 28). We found that the average mab-5 expression level was similar in QL and QR (p > 0.1, t-test). Importantly, we observed that mab-5 expression correlated with the position of the Q neuroblasts on the anteroposterior axis after initial migration. Thus, mab-5 transcript counts were significantly higher in posteriorly positioned Q neuroblasts than in Q neuroblasts that had migrated toward the anterior."
Reference	"WBPaper00040419"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00003102"

