Pattern	"GFP was seen in 100 to 200 cell embryos onwards, in many nuclei. GFP expression in the DVA neuron was apparent from the L1 to the mature adult. Intestinal expression of GFP was seen from the L1 or L2 to adult but the level of GFP in this tissue decreased in more mature adults. Many neurons in the head, and some in tail, also expressed GFP. GFP expression was present throughout the ventral nerve cord in the L1 and L2. The M cell expressed GFP in the L1 and and this continued into the resulting sex muscle precursors in later stages. GFP was also observed in body wall muscle. GFP expression in UL3704 was much fainter than in UL3705 and was only visible in DVA in most individuals."
Reference	"WBPaper00042262"
