Subcellular_localization	"In the mitotically dividing nuclei of the distal region of the germ-line, PLK-2 is first detectable at the centrosomes. However, upon entry into meiotic prophase, PLK-2 then localizes to approximately three to five chromosome-associated aggregates at the nuclear periphery of leptotene-zygotene nuclei; these aggregates disappear as synapsis initiates, and PLK-2 then colocalizes with the synapsed chromosomes of pachytene nuclei. PLK-2 colocalizes with PLK-1 to the nuclear periphery in some NE-associated patches but is undetectable in others."

