Pattern	"ceh-63prom::gfp expression was observed clearly in a single neuron in the tail ganglion in hermaphrodites. We identified this cell as the interneuron DVC by differential interference contrast (DIC) microscopy.Expression of ceh-63prom::gfp in DVC can be detected in embryos from the comma stage, shortly after DVC is born at about 340 min after the first cell division and continues throughout the life of the animal. Expression was also observed in uterine wall cells but since the GFP was spread throughout the cells the exact cell identities were difficult to identify with this reporter gene fusion."
Reference	"WBPaper00040555"
Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00045215"
Reporter_gene	"[ceh-63prom::gfp] transcriptional fusion. The reporter fusion in pUL#JRH10H1 contained the entire 562 bp upstream intergenic region from the ceh-63 translation initiation codon to the termination codon of C02F12.4. --precise ends."
Reporter_gene
Transgene	"WBTransgene00010181"

