Reflects_endogenous_expression_of	"WBGene00003155"
Subcellular_localization	"GFP-MCM-3 became enriched on chromosomes during anaphase of meiosis II and during meta- phase and anaphase of mitosis. GFP-MCM-3 was also massively accumulated in pronuclei and nuclei during interphase and prophase. Worms expressing GFP-MCM-2 showed an identical localization to that of GFP-MCM-3 during the first embryonic cell cycle, consistent with both of them being part of the hexameric MCM- 2-7 complex. The pan-MCM antibodies also showed additional centrosome staining, which might either be unspecific or a result of the location of MCM subunits other than MCM-3 and MCM-7."

